          "id": "thm-ip-deterministic-minimax-lower-bound-on-source-balls",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "Deterministic minimax lower bound on power source balls",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $K:X\\to Y$ be compact between real or complex Hilbert spaces over the same scalar field, $\\nu,\\rho>0$, and let $X_{\\nu,\\rho}(K)$ be its power source ball. For any deterministic reconstruction map $A:Y\\to X$ and any $\\delta\\ge0$, define $E_\\delta(A):=\\sup\\{\\|A(Kx+\\eta)-x\\|_X:x\\in X_{\\nu,\\rho}(K),\\ \\eta\\in Y,\\ \\|\\eta\\|_Y\\le\\delta\\}$. Then $E_\\delta(A)\\ge\\varepsilon_K(X_{\\nu,\\rho}(K),\\delta)$, and therefore $\\inf_{A:Y\\to X}E_\\delta(A)\\ge\\varepsilon_K(X_{\\nu,\\rho}(K),\\delta)$. For any $M\\subseteq X$ with $0\\in M$, define the two-truth modulus $\\widetilde\\varepsilon_K(M,\\delta):=\\sup\\{\\|x_1-x_2\\|_X:x_1,x_2\\in M,\\ \\|K(x_1-x_2)\\|_Y\\le2\\delta\\}$. Then $\\widetilde\\varepsilon_K(X_{\\nu,\\rho}(K),\\delta)=2\\varepsilon_K(X_{\\nu,\\rho}(K),\\delta)$.",
