      ],
      "order": 3004,
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-ip-error-budget-for-computed-inversion",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Error budget for computed Tikhonov inversion",
          "deps": [
            "def-ip-compact-linear-inverse-model"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Christian Clason, Regularization of Inverse Problems: Lecture Notes, arXiv:2001.00617v2, Chapter 8",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.00617v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "Per Christian Hansen, Introduction to Inverse Problems, Chapter 5: Regularization Parameter Choice",
                "url": "https://people.compute.dtu.dk/pcha/DIP/chap5.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Tristan van Leeuwen and Christoph Brune, 10 Lectures on Inverse Problems and Imaging, Chapter 3",
                "url": "https://tristanvanleeuwen.github.io/IP_and_Im_Lectures/ip_function_spaces.html"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $X,Y$ be real or complex Hilbert spaces over the same scalar field, let\n$A:X\\to Y$ be a compact linear forward map (the closure of $A(B)$ is compact\nin $Y$ for every bounded set $B\\subseteq X$), and let $A_h:X\\to Y$ be a\nbounded linear discretized map with finite-dimensional range. For a datum\n$b\\in Y$, let $\\lambda>0$ be the coefficient of $\\|x\\|_X^2$ in the Tikhonov\nobjective $\\|Ax-b\\|_Y^2+\\lambda\\|x\\|_X^2$. Supply adjoints $A^*:Y\\to X$ and\n$A_h^*:Y\\to X$ satisfying\n$\\langle Ax,y\\rangle_Y=\\langle x,A^*y\\rangle_X$ and\n$\\langle A_hx,y\\rangle_Y=\\langle x,A_h^*y\\rangle_X$, where the inner products\nare linear in their first arguments. Assume the shifted normal operators\n$A^*A+\\lambda I_X$ and $A_h^*A_h+\\lambda I_X$ are bijective, and define\n$$R_\\lambda=(A^*A+\\lambda I_X)^{-1}A^*,\\qquad R_{\\lambda,h}=(A_h^*A_h+\\lambda I_X)^{-1}A_h^*.$$\n\nFor a truth $x^\\dagger\\in X$, data perturbation $e\\in Y$, and $\\delta\\ge0$\nwith $\\|e\\|\\le\\delta$, put\n$$y=Ax^\\dagger,\\qquad y_\\delta=y+e,\\qquad y_{h,\\delta}=A_hx^\\dagger+e,\\qquad d_h=(A-A_h)x^\\dagger=y_\\delta-y_{h,\\delta}.$$\nFor any returned output $\\widetilde x_h\\in X$, define its exact discrete\nnormal-equation residual by\n$$r_{h,h}=(A_h^*A_h+\\lambda I_X)\\widetilde x_h-A_h^*y_{h,\\delta}.$$\nThe five-channel error budget is the ordered tuple\n$(b_{\\mathrm{bias}},b_{\\mathrm{data}},b_{\\mathrm{operator}},b_{\\mathrm{pre}},b_{\\mathrm{solve}})$, where\n$$\\begin{aligned}b_{\\mathrm{bias}}&=x^\\dagger-R_\\lambda y,\\qquad b_{\\mathrm{data}}=R_\\lambda y-R_\\lambda y_\\delta,\\\\b_{\\mathrm{operator}}&=(R_\\lambda-R_{\\lambda,h})y_{h,\\delta},\\qquad b_{\\mathrm{pre}}=R_\\lambda d_h,\\\\b_{\\mathrm{solve}}&=R_{\\lambda,h}y_{h,\\delta}-\\widetilde x_h.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe five entries are, in order, the truth-bias, data-perturbation,\nregularized-operator, pre-inversion, and algebraic-solve error vectors.\nThe scalar total budget is the sum of the five channel norms. The raw\npre-inversion forward residual is $d_h$; its reconstruction contribution is\n$b_{\\mathrm{pre}}$. The operator channel measures the difference between the\nregularized exact and discretized operators. The solve channel measures the\nreturned output's difference from the exact discrete Tikhonov output. The\ndefinition supplies no rate or arithmetic residual certificate."
        },
        {
          "id": "prop-ip-regularized-output-error-splits-by-source",
