          "id": "ex-ip-cfm-low-imh-acceptance-with-accurate-means",
          "kind": "example",
          "title": "Posterior summaries close to DRAM with low independent-MH acceptance",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice for the general density-based Metropolis–Hastings interface. In the stationary-diffusion inverse-problem experiment with $m=256$ observations, noise variance $\\gamma^2=10^{-5}$, and $n_{KL}=128$ prior modes, use the baseline conditional-flow-matching MLP with 800 hidden units. The reported flow-matching independent-Metropolis–Hastings acceptance rates for four different true parameters are respectively $0.66\\%$, $11.21\\%$, $5.97\\%$, and $5.47\\%$. In this same experiment, the reported posterior means and 95\\% bands agree with the DRAM reference to between $0.8\\%$ and $1.8\\%$ in relative $L^2$. The first truth is a prior-predictive tail observation: its normalized radius is $2.53$, the median training radius is $0.85$, and only $0.12\\%$ of the two million training observations have a larger radius. This reported case shows that close posterior means and bands do not by themselves imply high independent-Metropolis–Hastings acceptance or establish full posterior accuracy.",
