          "statement": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be real Hilbert spaces and let $U\\subseteq X$ be a nonempty open set in the norm topology. A **nonlinear forward model on Hilbert spaces** is a map $F:U\\to Y$; no linearity is assumed, and linear maps are allowed as special cases. For $y\\in Y$, its exact solution set is\n\n$$S_F(y):=\\{x\\in U:F(x)=y\\}.$$\n\nA point $x^\\dagger\\in U$ generates the exact datum $y=F(x^\\dagger)$. When $F$ is Fréchet differentiable at $x\\in U$, write $F'(x):X\\to Y$ for its unique bounded real-linear derivative."
