              {
                "title": "Christian Clason, Regularization of Inverse Problems, Theorem 9.9",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.00617v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "Barbara Kaltenbacher, Frank Schöpfer, and Thomas Schuster, Iterative methods for nonlinear ill-posed problems in Banach spaces, Proposition 1",
                "url": "https://www.f08.uni-stuttgart.de/.content/media/downloads/Mathematik/mathematische_berichte/2008/2008-005.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$ be a nonempty open set, let $F:U\\to Y$ be a forward map, let $y\\in Y$, and let $x_0\\in X$. A point $x^\\dagger\\in U$ is an **$x_0$-minimum-norm solution** of $F(x)=y$ on $U$ if $F(x^\\dagger)=y$ and\n\n$$\\|x^\\dagger-x_0\\|\\le\\|x-x_0\\|\\qquad\\text{for every }x\\in U\\text{ with }F(x)=y.$$\n\nThis definition asserts no existence or uniqueness; it describes the minimizing property of a supplied exact solution. The minimum is global over the exact solution set on $U$, with distance measured from the specified reference point $x_0$."
        },
        {
          "id": "def-ip-tangential-cone-condition",
