          "statement": "Let $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$ be open, and let $F:U\\to Y$ be Fréchet differentiable at $x\\in U$. Suppose that for some $\\delta>0$ with $\\overline B_\\delta(x)\\subseteq U$ and some $0\\le\\eta<1$, the local tangential cone condition at $x$ holds on radius $\\delta$ with constant $\\eta$. Then for every $h\\in X$ with $\\|h\\|_X\\le\\delta$,\n\n$$\n(1-\\eta)\\,\\|F(x+h)-F(x)\\|_Y\\le\\|F'(x)h\\|_Y\\le(1+\\eta)\\,\\|F(x+h)-F(x)\\|_Y.\n$$"
