          "statement": "Let $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$ be open, and let $F:U\\to Y$ be Fréchet differentiable. Let $x_0\\in X$, $y\\in Y$, and let $x^\\dagger\\in U$ be an $x_0$-minimum-norm solution of $F(x)=y$ on $U$. Suppose that for some $\\delta>0$ the closed ball $\\overline B_\\delta(x^\\dagger)$ lies in $U$, the local tangential cone condition holds at $x^\\dagger$ on radius $\\delta$ with a constant $0\\le\\eta<1$, and\n\n$$x^\\dagger-x_0\\in\\ker(F'(x^\\dagger))^\\perp.$$\n\nThen every $x\\in\\overline B_\\delta(x^\\dagger)$ with $F(x)=y$ and $x\\ne x^\\dagger$ satisfies\n\n$$\\|x-x_0\\|_X>\\|x^\\dagger-x_0\\|_X.$$\n\nConsequently, $x^\\dagger$ is the unique $x_0$-minimum-norm solution among the exact solutions in $\\overline B_\\delta(x^\\dagger)$."
