          "statement": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $D\\subseteq X$ be a nonempty domain, and let $F:D\\to Y$ be a forward map. For a regularization parameter $\\alpha>0$, reference element $x_0\\in X$, and datum $y\\in Y$, the **nonlinear Tikhonov functional** is the map $J_{\\alpha,y,x_0}:D\\to[0,\\infty)$ defined by\n\n$$\nJ_{\\alpha,y,x_0}(x):=\\frac12\\|F(x)-y\\|_Y^2+\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\|x-x_0\\|_X^2\\qquad(x\\in D).\n$$\n\nA **global minimizer** is a point $x_\\alpha\\in D$ such that $J_{\\alpha,y,x_0}(x_\\alpha)\\le J_{\\alpha,y,x_0}(x)$ for every $x\\in D$. This definition asserts neither existence nor uniqueness."
