          "statement": "Let $\\psi:[0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$ be continuous, nondecreasing, concave, and satisfy $\\psi(0)=0$. Extend $g=-\\psi$ to $\\mathbb R$ by $g(s)=+\\infty$ for $s<0$, and define $H(q):=g^*(-q)=\\sup_{s\\ge0}(\\psi(s)-qs)$ for $q>0$, assuming the displayed suprema below are finite. For $c_1,c_2,C_3,\\alpha>0$ and $d,r,e\\ge0$, if\n\n$$c_1r+c_2\\alpha e\\le d+\\alpha\\psi(C_3r),$$\n\nthen\n\n$$e\\le\\frac1{c_2}\\left(\\frac d\\alpha+H\\!\\left(\\frac{c_1}{C_3\\alpha}\\right)\\right),\\qquad r\\le\\frac2{c_1}\\left(d+\\alpha H\\!\\left(\\frac{c_1}{2C_3\\alpha}\\right)\\right).$$"
