        {
          "id": "def-ip-product-tangential-cone-condition",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Product-type tangential cone condition",
          "deps": [
            "def-ip-nonlinear-forward-map",
            "def-frechet-derivative-between-banach-spaces",
            "def-ip-tangential-cone-condition"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "justified_by": [],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Christian Clason, Regularization of Inverse Problems, Assumption 11.10 and equation (11.23)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.00617v2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$ be open, and let\n$F:U\\to Y$ be continuously Fréchet differentiable, meaning that $F$ is\nFréchet differentiable at each point of $U$ and $x\\mapsto F'(x)$ is continuous\nin operator norm. For a subset $V\\subseteq U$ and a constant $c>0$, the\n**product-type tangential cone condition on $V$ with constant $c$** is the\nrequirement that, for every $x,\\tilde x\\in V$,\n\n$$\\|F(x)-F(\\tilde x)-F'(x)(x-\\tilde x)\\|_Y\\le c\\|x-\\tilde x\\|_X\\|F(x)-F(\\tilde x)\\|_Y.$$"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-ip-lm-product-condition-implies-range-approximation",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Product condition gives the LM range-approximation bound",
          "deps": [
            "def-ip-product-tangential-cone-condition",
            "def-ip-nonlinear-forward-map",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-frechet-derivative-between-banach-spaces",
            "cor-inner-product-induces-a-norm"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "justified_by": [],
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Christian Clason, Regularization of Inverse Problems, Assumption 11.10 and proof of Theorem 11.11",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.00617v2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$ be open, and let\n$F:U\\to Y$ be Fréchet differentiable at every point of $U$ with\n$x\\mapsto F'(x)$ continuous in operator norm. Let $V\\subseteq U$ and let\n$c>0$ be such that, for every $u,\\tilde u\\in V$,\n$$\\|F(u)-F(\\tilde u)-F'(u)(u-\\tilde u)\\|_Y\\le c\\|u-\\tilde u\\|_X\\|F(u)-F(\\tilde u)\\|_Y.$$\nSuppose\n$x^\\dagger,x\\in V$, $F(x^\\dagger)=y$, $\\|y^\\delta-y\\|_Y\\le\\delta$ with\n$\\delta\\ge0$, $\\tau>0$, and $\\|x-x^\\dagger\\|_X\\le e$. If\n$R:=\\|F(x)-y^\\delta\\|_Y>\\tau\\delta$, then\n\n$$\\|F'(x)(x^\\dagger-x)+F(x)-y^\\delta\\|_Y\\le\\frac{1+ce(1+\\tau)}{\\tau}R.$$\n\nIn particular, if $\\sigma\\in(0,1)$, $e\\le e_0$, and\n$$\\gamma:=\\frac{\\sigma\\tau}{1+ce_0(1+\\tau)}>1,$$\nthen\n$$\\|F'(x)(x^\\dagger-x)+F(x)-y^\\delta\\|_Y\\le\\frac{\\sigma}{\\gamma}R.$$"
        },
        {
          "id": "alg-ip-regularized-levenberg-marquardt",
          "kind": "algorithm",
          "title": "Regularized nonlinear Levenberg–Marquardt with discrepancy stopping",
          "deps": [
            "def-ip-nonlinear-forward-map",
            "def-frechet-derivative-between-banach-spaces",
            "def-ip-product-tangential-cone-condition",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint",
            "lem-hilbert-tikhonov-normal-operator-invertible"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 4,
          "justified_by": [
            "lem-ip-lm-step-existence-and-residual-forcing"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Christian Clason, Regularization of Inverse Problems, §11.2, equations (11.14)–(11.16)",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.00617v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "Barbara Kaltenbacher, Inverse Problems – Applications and Solution Strategies, PDF p. 63",
                "url": "https://me.aau.at/~bkaltenb/AD12_kaltenbacher.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$\nbe open, and let $F:U\\to Y$ be continuously Fréchet differentiable, meaning\nthat $F$ is Fréchet differentiable at each point of $U$ and\n$x\\mapsto F'(x)$ is continuous in operator norm. The input consists of an\ninitial point $x_0\\in U$, a datum $y^\\delta\\in Y$, a positive noise bound\n$\\delta>0$, a discrepancy factor $\\tau>1$, a forcing fraction $\\sigma\\in(0,1)$,\na range-approximation margin $\\gamma>1$, and a finite update budget\n$N_{\\max}\\in\\mathbb N_0:=\\{0,1,2,\\ldots\\}$. Assume an exact solution $x^\\dagger\\in U$ exists\nwith $F(x^\\dagger)=y$ and $\\|y^\\delta-y\\|_Y\\le\\delta$. At every state\n$x_n^\\delta$ before the discrepancy stop, the admissible local range condition\nis\n$$\\|F'(x_n^\\delta)(x^\\dagger-x_n^\\delta)+F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y\\le\\frac{\\sigma}{\\gamma}\\|F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y.$$\n\nFor $x_n^\\delta\\in U$ and $\\alpha>0$, define $h_{n,\\alpha}$ to be the unique\nglobal minimizer over $h\\in X$ of the regularized linearized least-squares\nobjective\n$$J_{n,\\alpha}(h):=\\frac12\\|F'(x_n^\\delta)h+F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y^2+\\frac\\alpha2\\|h\\|_X^2.$$\nEquivalently, it is the unique solution of\n$$\\bigl(F'(x_n^\\delta)^*F'(x_n^\\delta)+\\alpha I_X\\bigr)h_{n,\\alpha}=F'(x_n^\\delta)^*(y^\\delta-F(x_n^\\delta)).$$\nHere $I_X$ is the identity operator on $X$.\nThe forcing rule selects any $\\alpha_n>0$ for which\n$$\\|F'(x_n^\\delta)h_{n,\\alpha_n}+F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y=\\sigma\\|F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y,$$\nand sets $x_{n+1}^\\delta=x_n^\\delta+h_{n,\\alpha_n}$. The displayed range\ncondition is a sufficient condition for the forcing rule to have such a\nparameter; it is not an input to either linearized minimization problem.\n\nFor a finite run, inspect $n=0,1,\\ldots,N_{\\max}$ in order. If\n$x_n^\\delta\\notin U$, return $(x_n^\\delta,n,\\texttt{domain-failure})$. If\n$\\|F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y\\le\\tau\\delta$, return\n$(x_n^\\delta,n,\\texttt{discrepancy})$. If $n=N_{\\max}$, return\n$(x_n^\\delta,n,\\texttt{budget-exhausted})$. Otherwise request the exact\nregularized minimizer and a positive parameter satisfying the forcing rule.\nIf the exact minimizer cannot be certified, return\n$(x_n^\\delta,n,\\texttt{solve-unverified})$; if the parameter selector cannot\nreturn a positive parameter satisfying the displayed equality, return\n$(x_n^\\delta,n,\\texttt{forcing-unavailable})$. After both exact calls succeed,\nset $x_{n+1}^\\delta=x_n^\\delta+h_{n,\\alpha_n}$ and continue. Each return is a\ntriple of state, index, and status. No convergence claim is attached to the\nfailure statuses or to a budget-exhausted state."
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-ip-lm-step-existence-and-residual-forcing",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "The regularized LM step and residual-forcing parameter exist",
          "deps": [
            "alg-ip-regularized-levenberg-marquardt",
            "lem-ip-lm-product-condition-implies-range-approximation",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space",
            "cor-inner-product-induces-a-norm",
            "lem-hilbert-tikhonov-normal-operator-invertible",
            "thm-intermediate-value"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "justified_by": [],
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Christian Clason, Regularization of Inverse Problems, Theorem 11.8 and its proof",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.00617v2"
              },
              {
                "title": "Barbara Kaltenbacher, Inverse Problems – Applications and Solution Strategies, PDF p. 63",
                "url": "https://me.aau.at/~bkaltenb/AD12_kaltenbacher.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $T:X\\to Y$ be\na bounded linear operator, let $r\\in Y$ be nonzero, and let\n$\\sigma\\in(0,1)$ and $\\gamma>1$. Suppose that a fixed $v\\in X$ satisfies\n$$\\|Tv-r\\|_Y\\le\\frac{\\sigma}{\\gamma}\\|r\\|_Y.$$\nFor each $\\alpha>0$, the functional\n$$\\Phi_\\alpha(h):=\\frac12\\|Th-r\\|_Y^2+\\frac\\alpha2\\|h\\|_X^2\\qquad(h\\in X)$$\nhas the unique global minimizer\n$$h_\\alpha=(T^*T+\\alpha I_X)^{-1}T^*r,$$\nwhere $T^*$ is the Hilbert adjoint and $I_X$ is the identity on $X$. Moreover,\nthere exists at least one $\\alpha>0$ for which\n$$\\|Th_\\alpha-r\\|_Y=\\sigma\\|r\\|_Y.$$"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-ip-lm-fejer-decrease-and-parameter-bound",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Regularized LM decreases the local solution error",
          "deps": [
            "alg-ip-regularized-levenberg-marquardt",
            "lem-ip-lm-product-condition-implies-range-approximation",
            "lem-ip-lm-step-existence-and-residual-forcing",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint",
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space",
            "lem-of-abs-value",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-in-an-inner-product-space",
            "thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties",
            "cor-inner-product-induces-a-norm"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "justified_by": [],
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Christian Clason, Regularization of Inverse Problems, Lemma 11.9 and proof of Theorem 11.11",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.00617v2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $T:X\\to Y$ be\nbounded linear with Hilbert adjoint $T^*$, and let $e\\in X$ and\n$r\\in Y\\setminus\\{0\\}$. Suppose $0<\\sigma<1$, $\\gamma>1$, $\\alpha>0$,\nand $h$ is the unique minimizer of\n$$h\\longmapsto\\frac12\\|Th-r\\|_Y^2+\\frac\\alpha2\\|h\\|_X^2.$$\nAssume its residual forcing and the range-approximation condition are\n$$\\|Th-r\\|_Y=\\sigma\\|r\\|_Y,$$\n$$\\|Te+r\\|_Y\\le\\frac\\sigma\\gamma\\|r\\|_Y.$$\nThen\n$$\\|e\\|_X^2-\\|e+h\\|_X^2\\ge\\|h\\|_X^2+\\frac{2(\\gamma-1)\\sigma^2}{\\gamma\\alpha}\\|r\\|_Y^2.$$\nIf also $\\|T\\|\\le M$ for some $M>0$, then\n$$\\alpha\\le\\frac{\\sigma M^2}{1-\\sigma}.$$"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-ip-lm-local-discrepancy-stopping",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "Local regularized LM discrepancy stopping has logarithmic iteration count",
          "deps": [
            "alg-ip-regularized-levenberg-marquardt",
            "def-ip-nonlinear-forward-map",
            "def-hilbert-space",
            "def-frechet-derivative-between-banach-spaces",
            "def-operator-norm",
            "def-ip-product-tangential-cone-condition",
            "lem-ip-lm-product-condition-implies-range-approximation",
            "lem-ip-lm-fejer-decrease-and-parameter-bound",
            "lem-ip-lm-step-existence-and-residual-forcing",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "cor-inner-product-induces-a-norm",
            "def-natural-logarithm",
            "thm-natural-logarithm-laws",
            "lem-cauchy-reals-archimedean"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 7,
          "justified_by": [],
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Christian Clason, Regularization of Inverse Problems, Assumption 11.10 and Theorem 11.11 with complete proof",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.00617v2"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$\nbe open, and let $F:U\\to Y$ be Fréchet differentiable everywhere with\n$x\\mapsto F'(x)$ continuous in operator norm. For $s>0$, write\n$$B_s(x_0):=\\{x\\in X:\\|x-x_0\\|_X<s\\}.$$\nSuppose $B_{2r}(x_0)\\subseteq U$ for some $r>0$, $x^\\dagger\\in B_r(x_0)$,\nand $F(x^\\dagger)=y$. Assume there are constants $M,c>0$ such that, for every\n$x,\\tilde x\\in B_{2r}(x_0)$,\n$$\\|F'(x)\\|\\le M,$$\n$$\\|F(x)-F(\\tilde x)-F'(x)(x-\\tilde x)\\|_Y\\le c\\|x-\\tilde x\\|_X\\|F(x)-F(\\tilde x)\\|_Y.$$\nFix $\\sigma\\in(0,1)$ and $\\tau>1/\\sigma$. Put\n$$e_0:=\\|x_0-x^\\dagger\\|_X$$\nand assume\n$$e_0<\\min\\left\\{r,\\frac{\\sigma\\tau-1}{c(1+\\tau)},\\frac{1-\\sigma}{2c}\\right\\}.$$\nSet\n$$\\gamma:=\\frac{\\sigma\\tau}{1+ce_0(1+\\tau)};$$\nthe hypotheses give $\\gamma>1$. For each exact iteration, use this $\\gamma$ in\nthe range-approximation margin of the regularized LM procedure and select any\npositive parameter satisfying its residual-forcing equality.\nFor every $\\delta>0$ and $y^\\delta\\in Y$ satisfying\n$\\|y^\\delta-y\\|_Y\\le\\delta$, start at $x_0^\\delta=x_0$ and, at each state\nbefore stopping, let $h_n$ minimize\n$$h\\longmapsto\\frac12\\|F'(x_n^\\delta)h+F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y^2+\\frac{\\alpha_n}{2}\\|h\\|_X^2$$\nfor a selected $\\alpha_n>0$ satisfying\n$$\\|F'(x_n^\\delta)h_n+F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y=\\sigma\\|F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y,$$\nand set $x_{n+1}^\\delta=x_n^\\delta+h_n$. Let $N_\\delta$ be the first\n$n\\in\\mathbb N_0:=\\{0,1,2,\\ldots\\}$ such that\n$$\\|F(x_n^\\delta)-y^\\delta\\|_Y\\le\\tau\\delta.$$\nThen this exact iteration is well-defined up to a finite first discrepancy\nindex $N_\\delta$. Set\n$$q:=\\frac{\\sigma+ce_0}{1-ce_0},\\qquad K:=1+\\|F(x_0)-y\\|_Y,\\qquad \\delta_0:=\\min\\left\\{1,\\frac K\\tau\\right\\}.$$\nHere $q\\in(0,1)$ and $\\log$ denotes the natural logarithm. For\n$0<\\delta\\le\\delta_0$,\n$$N_\\delta\\le1+\\frac{\\log(K/(\\tau\\delta))}{-\\log q}.$$\nConsequently $N_\\delta=O(1+|\\log\\delta|)$ as $\\delta\\downarrow0$, with\nconstants depending only on the fixed problem and displayed parameters. A\nfinite run with update budget at least $N_\\delta$ and successful exact calls\nreturns this first crossing; a shorter budget may return\n`budget-exhausted`. No convergence rate for $x_{N_\\delta}^\\delta$ is asserted."
        }
      ]
    }

