        {
          "id": "def-ip-tv-variational-curvature",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Variational curvature of a finite-perimeter set",
          "deps": [
            "def-ip-spatial-bv-and-distributional-tv",
            "def-ip-boundary-tv-conventions"
          ],
          "statement": "Let $\\Omega=\\mathbb R^2$ or let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain. Choose one of three perimeter functionals for measurable $E\\subseteq\\Omega$: full-space perimeter $P_R(E)=P(E;\\mathbb R^2)$ when $\\Omega=\\mathbb R^2$; Neumann relative perimeter $P_N(E)=P(E;\\Omega)$ on a bounded domain; or Dirichlet perimeter $P_D(E)=P(\\widetilde E;\\mathbb R^2)$, where $\\widetilde E$ is $E$ extended by the empty set outside $\\Omega$. Require finite measure and finite selected perimeter, and let $\\kappa:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ be Lebesgue-measurable with $\\int_F|\\kappa|<\\infty$ for every set considered. The set $E$ has **variational curvature** $\\kappa$ for the selected model if its selected perimeter minus $\\int_E\\kappa\\,dx$ is no greater than the same quantity for every finite-measure finite-selected-perimeter competitor $F\\subseteq\\Omega$ whose symmetric difference $F\\mathbin\\triangle E$ has compact closure in $\\Omega$. In the full-space model, this means compact closure in $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\nFor bounded Dirichlet TV, a separate **obstacle curvature** condition on $\\Omega$ means that $\\Omega$, viewed as a finite-perimeter set in $\\mathbb R^2$, minimizes $F\\mapsto P(F;\\mathbb R^2)-\\int_F\\kappa_\\Omega\\,dx$ over all finite-measure finite-perimeter $F\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ whose symmetric difference with $\\Omega$ has compact closure in $\\mathbb R^2$, where $\\kappa_\\Omega\\in L^1(\\mathbb R^2;\\mathbb R)$.",
          "sources": {
