          "statement": "Let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ be open and let $TV_2(\\cdot;\\Omega)$ be the extended distributional total variation on $L^2(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$. It is proper, convex, lower semicontinuous in the $L^2$ norm, and positively one-homogeneous for nonnegative scalars. For every $u\\in BV(\\Omega)\\cap L^2(\\Omega)$, it agrees with spatial TV: $TV_2(u;\\Omega)=TV(u;\\Omega)$.",
