          ],
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. If $u\\in L^2(\\mathbb R^2;\\mathbb R)$ and $TV_2(u;\\mathbb R^2)<\\infty$, there exist smooth cutoffs $\\chi_k$ with $0\\le\\chi_k\\le1$, $\\chi_k=1$ on $B(0,k)$, support in $B(0,2k)$, and $\\sup_{k\\ge1}k\\|\\nabla\\chi_k\\|_\\infty<\\infty$. For every family satisfying these four conditions, $v_k:=\\chi_ku$ belongs to $BV(\\mathbb R^2)\\cap L^1(\\mathbb R^2)$, has support in $B(0,2k)$, converges to $u$ in $L^2(\\mathbb R^2)$, and\n$$\\limsup_{k\\to\\infty}TV(v_k;\\mathbb R^2)\\le TV_2(u;\\mathbb R^2).$$",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "José A. Iglesias, Gwenael Mercier, and Otmar Scherzer, A note on convergence of solutions of total variation regularized linear inverse problems, §1.1",
