        {
          "id": "lem-ip-tv-dual-attainment-and-certificate-limit",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Dual attainment and convergence of TV source certificates",
          "deps": [
            "def-ip-tv-dual-source-certificate",
            "def-ip-bregman-distance",
            "def-ip-spatial-bv-and-distributional-tv",
            "def-ip-boundary-tv-conventions",
            "def-ip-banach-convex-subgradient-and-dual-pairing",
            "def-ip-variational-source-condition",
            "lem-ip-banach-fenchel-duality-for-regularization",
            "thm-ip-vsc-nonlinear-regularization-rate",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-in-an-inner-product-space",
            "thm-bolzano-weierstrass",
            "thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space"
          ],
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $X=L^2(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$ and $Y=L^2(\\Sigma,\\mu;\\mathbb R)$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $A:X\\to Y$ be bounded and real-linear, and let $R:X\\to[0,+\\infty]$ be one of the full-space, Dirichlet, or Neumann TV functionals. Assume that $R$ is proper, convex, lower semicontinuous, and positively one-homogeneous, and that $u^\\dagger$ is a minimum-$R$ exact solution of $Au=f$ with a dual source certificate $p^\\dagger\\in Y$, so $A^*p^\\dagger\\in\\partial R(u^\\dagger)$. Define $K:=\\{p\\in Y:A^*p\\in\\partial R(0)\\}$ and $D_{\\alpha,w}(p):=\\langle f+w,p\\rangle_Y-\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\|p\\|_Y^2$ for $\\alpha>0$ and $w\\in Y$.\n\nFor each $\\alpha>0$ and $w\\in Y$, $D_{\\alpha,w}$ has a unique maximizer on $K$, namely $p_{\\alpha,w}=\\operatorname{Proj}_K((f+w)/\\alpha)$. If $u_{\\alpha,w}$ is any supplied global minimizer of $u\\mapsto\\frac12\\|Au-(f+w)\\|_Y^2+\\alpha R(u)$, then $p_{\\alpha,w}=(f+w-Au_{\\alpha,w})/\\alpha$, $A^*p_{\\alpha,w}\\in\\partial R(u_{\\alpha,w})$, and $A^*p_{\\alpha,w}\\in\\partial R(0)$. For every such supplied minimizer, the correctly normalized primal-dual value identity is\n\n$$\\min_u\\{\\tfrac12\\|Au-(f+w)\\|_Y^2+\\alpha R(u)\\}=\\alpha D_{\\alpha,w}(p_{\\alpha,w}).$$\n\nLet $P_0:=\\{p\\in K:\\langle f,p\\rangle_Y=R(u^\\dagger)\\}$ and let $p_0$ be its unique minimum-norm element. For every sequence $\\alpha_n>0$ with $\\alpha_n\\to0$, $p_{\\alpha_n,0}\\to p_0$ strongly in $Y$ and $A^*p_{\\alpha_n,0}\\to A^*p_0$ strongly in $X$. For every $\\alpha>0$ and $w\\in Y$,\n\n$$\\|p_{\\alpha,w}-p_{\\alpha,0}\\|_Y\\le\\frac{\\|w\\|_Y}{\\alpha},\\qquad \\|A^*p_{\\alpha,w}-A^*p_{\\alpha,0}\\|_X\\le\\frac{\\|A^*\\|\\,\\|w\\|_Y}{\\alpha}.$$\n\nMoreover, for any $R_0>R(u^\\dagger)$ the certificate yields a variational source condition on $\\{u:R(u)\\le R_0\\}$ with exponent $2$, coefficient $\\beta=0$, and index function $\\psi(s)=(1+\\|p^\\dagger\\|_Y)\\sqrt{s}$. Consequently, if $\\delta_n\\downarrow0$, $\\|w_n\\|_Y\\le\\delta_n$, $\\alpha_n\\asymp\\delta_n$, and exact global minimizers $u_n$ are supplied, then the variational-source rate theorem gives\n\n$$D_R^{A^*p^\\dagger}(u_n,u^\\dagger)=O(\\delta_n),\\qquad \\|Au_n-(f+w_n)\\|_Y=O(\\delta_n).$$",
          "sources": {
