          "statement": "Let $m,n,s\\in\\mathbb N$ with $m,n\\ge1$ and $1\\le s\\le n$, let $A\\in\\mathbb R^{m\\times n}$, and let $0<\\rho<1$ and $\\tau>0$. In real scalar expressions, a natural number denotes its canonical real image. Use one-based coordinate labels $[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$, identifying coordinate label $j$ with library coordinate $j-1$. For $h\\in\\mathbb R^n$ and $S\\subseteq[n]$, let $h_S$ agree with $h$ on $S$ and vanish on $S^c=[n]\\setminus S$. The matrix $A$ satisfies the **$\\ell^2$ robust nullspace property of order $s$ with constants $(\\rho,\\tau)$** if\n$$\\|h_S\\|_2\\le \\frac{\\rho}{\\sqrt{s}}\\|h_{S^c}\\|_1+\\tau\\|Ah\\|_2$$\nfor every $h\\in\\mathbb R^n$ and every $S\\subseteq[n]$ with $|S|\\le s$. This condition applies to all vectors, including vectors with $Ah\\ne0$.",
