          },
          "sources": {
            "scraped": [],
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "P.-A. Absil, R. Mahony, and R. Sepulchre, Optimization Algorithms on Matrix Manifolds, Chapter 4 (2008)",
                "url": "https://assets.press.princeton.edu/chapters/absil/Absil_Chap4.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Nicolas Boumal, An Introduction to Optimization on Smooth Manifolds (2023 prepublication)",
                "url": "https://www.nicolasboumal.net/book/IntroOptimManifolds_Boumal_2023.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "For the supplied $C^1$ objective and ambient gradient oracle, the displayed projected vector is the Frobenius metric-dual gradient of the restricted objective, and every polar trial is defined. For every input satisfying the finite-budget Stiefel gradient procedure, it returns after at most $K$ trial evaluations with an output frame $X_{\\rm out}\\in\\operatorname{St}(n,p)$. Every accepted update has nonincreasing objective value, and the returned status is `target-met` exactly when $r(X_{\\rm out})\\le\\tau$; every other returned status has $r(X_{\\rm out})>\\tau$."
        }
      ]
