          "statement": "Discretize $-u''=f$ on $(0,1)$ with $u(0)=u(1)=0$ using grid points $x_i=i/3$ for $i=0,1,2,3$ and the two interior values $u_i=u(x_i)$, $z=(u_1,u_2)$. Put $h=1/3$ and define the centered stencil at $i=1,2$ by $D_hu_i=(2u_i-u_{i-1}-u_{i+1})/h^2$, with boundary values $u_0=u_3=0$. The resulting finite-difference system is $A_hz=f_h$, where $A_h=h^{-2}\\begin{pmatrix}2&-1\\\\-1&2\\end{pmatrix}$ and $f_h=(f(x_1),f(x_2))$. Use parameter and data spaces $X=Y=\\mathbb R^2$ with their Euclidean metrics, take $U=X$, and use the linear forward map $A_h|_U:U\\to Y$. Impose the physical constraint $C=\\{(z_1,z_2)\\in\\mathbb R^2:z_1\\ge0,\\ z_2\\ge0\\}$ for nonnegative nodal concentration. An input validator that checks both coordinates before invoking the linear solver rejects the candidate $z=(-1,1)$ before solving because its first coordinate is negative."
