              {
                "title": "Frank Natterer, X-ray Tomography, in Inverse Problems and Imaging",
                "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/profile/Frank-Natterer/publication/226521751_X-ray_Tomography/links/02e7e525392792a0a3000000/X-ray-Tomography.pdf",
                "locator": "§2.1, pp. 18–20, Theorem 2.1: projection-slice theorem and line-coordinate proof."
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "For every $f\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^2;\\mathbb C)$, every unit normal $\\theta\\in S^1$, and every $\\sigma\\in\\mathbb R$, the compact-support Fourier transform of the line data in the offset variable equals the restriction of the two-dimensional Fourier transform to the line in frequency space with direction $\\theta$:\n$$\\widehat{Rf}(\\theta,\\sigma)=\\widehat f(\\sigma\\theta).$$"
        },
        {
          "id": "thm-ip-radon-normal-operator",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "The Euclidean Radon normal operator and inversion formula",
          "deps": [
