          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Mikko Salo, RICAM lecture notes v1, §2.1: Radon transform in R²",
                "url": "https://users.jyu.fi/~salomi/lecturenotes/RICAM_notes_v1.pdf",
                "locator": "§2.1, pp. 4–7: normal operator, polar-coordinate calculation, and filtered-backprojection formula."
              },
              {
                "title": "Frank Natterer, X-ray Tomography, in Inverse Problems and Imaging",
                "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/profile/Frank-Natterer/publication/226521751_X-ray_Tomography/links/02e7e525392792a0a3000000/X-ray-Tomography.pdf",
                "locator": "§2.1, pp. 18–20, Theorems 2.1–2.2 and formula (7): slice theorem and two-dimensional inversion formula."
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\mu$ be the polar surface measure on $S^1$, defined on Borel $E\\subseteq S^1$ by\n$$\\mu(E):=2\\lambda_2\\bigl(\\{r\\theta:\\theta\\in E,\\ 0<r\\le1\\}\\bigr),$$\nwhere $\\lambda_2$ is Lebesgue measure on $\\mathbb R^2$. For continuous $g:S^1\\times\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb C$ for which the integral exists, define its **backprojection** by\n$$R^*g(x):=\\int_{S^1}g(\\theta,x\\cdot\\theta)\\,d\\mu(\\theta).$$\nFor every $f\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^2;\\mathbb C)$ and every $x\\in\\mathbb R^2$, the normal-operator and filtered-backprojection identities hold:\n$$R^*Rf(x)=4\\pi|D|^{-1}f(x),\\qquad f(x)=\\frac1{4\\pi}R^*|D_s|Rf(x),$$\nwith $|D|^{-1}$ and $|D_s|$ as defined for the compact-support Fourier convention in the Euclidean Radon transform definition."
        },
        {
          "id": "alg-ip-filtered-backprojection-complete-data",
          "kind": "algorithm",
          "title": "Complete-data filtered backprojection",
          "deps": [
            "def-ip-2d-radon-transform",
            "thm-ip-fourier-slice-identity",
            "thm-ip-radon-normal-operator"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 3,
          "justified_by": [],
          "forward_refs": [],
          "provenance": {
