          "statement": "Define $\\eta(u)=0$ for $u\\le0$ and $\\eta(u)=e^{-1/u}$ for $u>0$, and put $f(x)=\\eta(1-|x|^2)$ on $\\mathbb R^2$. This is a nonzero, smooth, compactly supported radial phantom. Its Euclidean Radon transform is independent of $\\theta$ and is\n$$Rf(\\theta,s)=\\begin{cases}\\displaystyle\\int_{-\\sqrt{1-s^2}}^{\\sqrt{1-s^2}}\\eta(1-s^2-t^2)\\,dt,&|s|<1,\\\\[1.2ex]0,&|s|\\ge1.\\end{cases}$$"
