          "statement": "Let $(M,g)$ be a compact, connected, nonempty smooth Riemannian surface with smooth boundary, and assume its boundary is strictly convex, it has no conjugate points, and it is nontrapping. Let $\\pi:\\widetilde M\\to M$ be the tangent orientation double cover, give $\\widetilde M$ the pullback metric $\\widetilde g=\\pi^*g$, and let $C$ be any connected component of $\\widetilde M$. Then $C$ is a compact, connected, oriented simple Riemannian surface with smooth boundary, and $\\pi|_C:C\\to M$ is a local isometry mapping $\\partial C$ onto $\\partial M$. For every $f\\in C_c^\\infty(M^\\circ)$, define $\\widetilde f=f\\circ\\pi$. For each incoming unit vector $\\widetilde z\\in\\partial_+SC$, the scalar geodesic X-ray transform satisfies\n$$\nI_{0,C}\\widetilde f(\\widetilde z)=I_{0,M}f(\\pi(\\widetilde z)).\n$$\nIn particular, zero data for $f$ on $M$ gives zero data for $\\widetilde f$ on every component $C$."
