          "statement": "Let $(M,g)$ be a compact, connected, nonempty, oriented smooth Riemannian surface with smooth strictly convex boundary, no conjugate points, and nontrapping geodesic flow. Set $SM=\\{(x,v):x\\in M,\\ g_x(v,v)=1\\}$ and let $\\varphi_t$ be the unit-speed geodesic flow until boundary exit. For $w\\in C^\\infty(SM,\\mathbb R)$ define $Xw=\\left.\\frac{d}{dt}\\right|_{0}w(\\varphi_t(x,v))$. Define $Vw(x,v)=\\left.\\frac{d}{d\\theta}\\right|_{0}w(x,\\cos\\theta\\,v+\\sin\\theta\\,v^\\perp)$, where $v^\\perp$ is the positive $90$-degree rotation of $v$, and set $X^\\perp=[X,V]$. For a positive orthonormal frame $e_1,e_2$, let $K(x)=g(R(e_1,e_2)e_2,e_1)$, where $R(A,B)C=\\nabla_A\\nabla_BC-\\nabla_B\\nabla_AC-\\nabla_{[A,B]}C$; this value is independent of the frame. Let $d\\Sigma=dV_g(x)\\,dS_x(v)$ be the Liouville measure and define $(a,b)=\\int_{SM}ab\\,d\\Sigma$ and $\\|a\\|^2=(a,a)$. For every real-valued $u\\in C^\\infty(SM)$ with $u=0$ on $\\partial SM$,\n$$\n\\|VXu\\|^2=\\|XVu\\|^2-(KVu,Vu)+\\|Xu\\|^2.\n$$"
