          "statement": "Let $(M,g)$ be a compact, nonempty smooth Riemannian manifold with smooth boundary, let $T>0$, set $Q=(0,T)\\times M$ and $\\Sigma=(0,T)\\times\\partial M$, and let $\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}}$ be the outward unit normal. Write $\\nabla_g u$ for the metric gradient, $\\Delta_g u=\\operatorname{div}_g\\nabla_g u$, $dV_g$ for Riemannian volume, and $dS_g$ for the induced boundary measure. The $C^1$ norms below are computed in any fixed finite smooth atlas of the indicated compact sets. For $u,v\\in C^2([0,T]\\times M)$,\n$$\\int_Q\\big((\\partial_t^2-\\Delta_g)u\\,v-u(\\partial_t^2-\\Delta_g)v\\big)\\,dV_gdt =\\int_\\Sigma\\big(u\\,\\partial_{\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}}}v-v\\,\\partial_{\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}}}u\\big)\\,dS_gdt +\\int_M[\\partial_tu\\,v-u\\,\\partial_tv]_{t=0}^{t=T}\\,dV_g.$$\nFor every $h\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Sigma)$ there is a smooth lift $H$ on $[0,T]\\times M$ with $H|_\\Sigma=h$, supported in a fixed boundary collar and zero near $t=0,T$, such that $\\|H\\|_{C^1([0,T]\\times M)}\\le C\\|h\\|_{C^1(\\Sigma)}$. For every $u\\in C^1([0,T]\\times M)$ the classical normal trace obeys\n$$\\|\\partial_{\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}}}u\\|_{L^2(\\Sigma)}\\le \\big(T\\,\\operatorname{area}_g(\\partial M)\\big)^{1/2}\\|\\nabla_g u\\|_{C^0([0,T]\\times M)}.$$"
