          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $(M,g)$ be a compact, connected, nonempty smooth Riemannian manifold with nonempty smooth boundary, let $T>0$, and let $q_1,q_2\\in C^\\infty(M;\\mathbb R)$ be time independent. Put $Q_0=\\operatorname{supp}(q_1-q_2)$, the closure of the set on which $q_1-q_2$ is nonzero, and suppose $Q_0\\ne\\varnothing$ and $d_g(Q_0,\\partial M)>T/2$, where $d_g$ is the intrinsic Riemannian distance. For every smooth Dirichlet input $h\\in C_c^\\infty((0,T)\\times\\partial M)$, the full time-dependent forward Dirichlet-to-Neumann maps satisfy\n$$\\Lambda_{q_1}^+h=\\Lambda_{q_2}^+h\\quad\\text{in }L^2((0,T)\\times\\partial M,dS_gdt).$$\nThus a perturbation supported farther than half the observation time from the boundary cannot be detected by boundary measurements made before time $T$."
