          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $n\\ge2$, let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^n$ be a bounded connected domain with smooth nonempty boundary, and regard $\\overline\\Omega$ as a compact smooth manifold with the Euclidean metric. Write $H^1_{\\rm E}(\\Omega)=W^{1,2}(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$ and let $H^1_{0,\\rm E}(\\Omega)$ be the closure of $C_c^\\infty(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$ in that norm; put $\\mathcal B_{\\rm E}:=H^1_{\\rm E}(\\Omega)/H^1_{0,\\rm E}(\\Omega)$. Let $H^1_{\\rm fix}(\\overline\\Omega)$ and $H^1_{0,\\rm fix}(\\overline\\Omega)$ be the fixed-atlas spaces on $\\overline\\Omega$ and let $H^{1/2}_{\\rm fix}(\\partial\\Omega)$ be the fixed-atlas boundary space using localized Euclidean $W^{1/2,2}$ norms. The identity on smooth functions extends to bounded linear isomorphisms between $H^1_{\\rm E}(\\Omega)$ and $H^1_{\\rm fix}(\\overline\\Omega)$, and between their zero-boundary subspaces. Classical boundary restriction extends to a bounded linear trace $T:H^1_{\\rm fix}(\\overline\\Omega)\\to H^{1/2}_{\\rm fix}(\\partial\\Omega)$ with kernel $H^1_{0,\\rm fix}(\\overline\\Omega)$. The induced quotient map is a bounded linear isomorphism\n\n$$H^1_{\\rm E}(\\Omega)/H^1_{0,\\rm E}(\\Omega)\\;\\cong\\;H^1_{\\rm fix}(\\overline\\Omega)/H^1_{0,\\rm fix}(\\overline\\Omega)\\;\\cong\\;H^{1/2}_{\\rm fix}(\\partial\\Omega).$$\n\nThus the Euclidean trace quotient and the fixed-atlas $H^{1/2}$ boundary space are canonically equivalent."
