          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice, and let $n\\ge3$. Let $M$ be a compact connected smooth $n$-manifold with nonempty smooth boundary and no orientability assumption, and let $\\Gamma\\subsetneq\\partial M$ be a nonempty relatively open patch. Use a fixed finite smooth atlas and subordinate smooth partition of unity. Define $H^1(M)$ as the completion of $C^\\infty(M)$ under the sum of localized Euclidean $W^{1,2}$ norms. For each integer $k\\ge0$, $H^k(M)$ uses the same completion convention with localized $W^{k,2}$ norms. Let $H_0^1(M)$ be the closure of $C_c^\\infty(M^\\circ)$ in $H^1(M)$. Define $H^{1/2}(\\partial M)$ by the same fixed boundary atlas and partition, using localized Euclidean $W^{1/2,2}$ Slobodeckij norms. Let $\\operatorname{Tr}:H^1(M)\\to H^{1/2}(\\partial M)$ be the Sobolev trace, the continuous extension of classical boundary restriction. For a smooth Riemannian metric $g$, write $dV_g=\\sqrt{\\det(g_{ij})}\\,|dx^1\\cdots dx^n|$ in coordinates and let $dS_g$ be its induced boundary density; $\\langle du,dv\\rangle_g$ is the cotangent inner product induced by $g^{-1}$. For $f\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Gamma)$ extended by zero on $\\partial M\\setminus\\Gamma$, let $u_{g,f}\\in H^1(M)$ be the unique weak solution with $\\operatorname{Tr}u_{g,f}=f$ and\n\n$$\\int_M\\langle du_{g,f},dv\\rangle_g\\,dV_g=0\\qquad(v\\in H_0^1(M)).$$\n\nThe zero-boundary kernel is trivial by uniqueness of the positive scalar Dirichlet problem, so the nonresonant elliptic regularity interface applies; for smooth $f$, the solution lies in every integer-order Sobolev space. This is the positive scalar conductivity Dirichlet problem at $\\gamma\\equiv1$. Define its local zero-frequency energy map, with the same patch for inputs and observations, by\n\n$$\\mathcal E_{g,\\Gamma}(f,h):=\\int_M\\langle du_{g,f},du_{g,h}\\rangle_g\\,dV_g\\qquad(f,h\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Gamma)).$$\n\nThe displayed energy is the weak scalar DN pairing with the second extension chosen as $u_{g,h}$. If two smooth metrics $g_1,g_2$ on this same manifold satisfy $\\mathcal E_{g_1,\\Gamma}(f,h)=\\mathcal E_{g_2,\\Gamma}(f,h)$ for every such pair, must there be a smooth diffeomorphism $\\Phi:M\\to M$ with $\\Phi|_\\Gamma=\\operatorname{id}$ and $g_2=\\Phi^*g_1$, where $(\\Phi^*g_1)_p(v,w):=(g_1)_{\\Phi(p)}(D\\Phi_pv,D\\Phi_pw)$?"
