          "axiom_use": "No choice axiom is used; the finite termination claim is conditional on the model's supplied finite-return routines.",
          "statement": "For any finite-element PDE model satisfying its solver and admissibility contract, the finite-budget Tikhonov algorithm returns after finitely many operations one of `converged`, `discrepancy-stopped`, `linear-solve-failed`, `inadmissible`, or `budget-exhausted`. A `converged` return satisfies the exact discrete projected-gradient bound $\\|G_L(q)\\|_2\\le\\tau_g$; a `discrepancy-stopped` return satisfies $\\|F_h(q)-y^\\delta\\|_{Y_h}\\le\\kappa\\delta$. Every accepted safeguarded step has nonincreasing exact discrete objective $\\Phi_h$. `inadmissible` and `linear-solve-failed` are returned only on the corresponding failed predicate or solver-certificate checks. `budget-exhausted` asserts no optimizer or continuous-model accuracy."
