          "title": "Exact Gaussian credible-ball coverage with a score-error budget of zero",
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, $\\sigma,\\tau>0$, and $0<\\gamma<1$. Given a scalar truth $\\theta\\in\\mathbb R$, observe independent $Y_i\\sim N(\\theta,\\sigma^2)$, $i=1,\\ldots,n$, and use the proper prior $\\theta\\sim N(0,\\tau^2)$. Write $\\bar Y=n^{-1}\\sum_iY_i$, $v_n=(\\tau^{-2}+n\\sigma^{-2})^{-1}$, $a_n=v_n n\\sigma^{-2}$, and $z_\\gamma=\\Phi^{-1}(1-\\gamma/2)$, where $\\Phi$ is the standard normal cumulative distribution function. The exact posterior is $N(a_n\\bar Y,v_n)$ and its central $(1-\\gamma)$ credible interval is $C_n(\\bar Y)=[a_n\\bar Y-z_\\gamma\\sqrt{v_n},a_n\\bar Y+z_\\gamma\\sqrt{v_n}]$. Its frequentist coverage at truth $\\theta$ is\n$$P_\\theta\\{\\theta\\in C_n(\\bar Y)\\}=\\Phi\\!\\left(\\frac{z_\\gamma\\sqrt{v_n}+(1-a_n)\\theta}{a_n\\sigma/\\sqrt n}\\right)-\\Phi\\!\\left(\\frac{-z_\\gamma\\sqrt{v_n}+(1-a_n)\\theta}{a_n\\sigma/\\sqrt n}\\right).$$",
