          "statement": "Fix $R,a_0,\\sigma>0$ and $0\\le\\rho_A<a_0/2$. The working inverse is $g(y)=y/a_0$. Under a test operator $a=a_0+\\delta$ with $|\\delta|\\le\\rho_A$, the observation is $Y=a\\theta+\\varepsilon$ for $\\theta\\in[-R,R]$ and independent $\\varepsilon\\sim N(0,\\sigma^2)$. For any two truth laws $\\mu_0,\\mu$ on $[-R,R]$, define $W_1(\\mu,\\mu_0)$ as the infimum of $E|\\Theta-\\Theta_0|$ over their couplings. The risk is\n$$R_{\\mu,\\delta}(g)=E_{\\theta\\sim\\mu,\\varepsilon}|g((a_0+\\delta)\\theta+\\varepsilon)-\\theta|^2=\\frac{\\delta^2}{a_0^2}E_\\mu\\theta^2+\\frac{\\sigma^2}{a_0^2},$$\nand it satisfies $R_{\\mu,\\delta}(g)\\le(\\rho_A^2R^2+\\sigma^2)/a_0^2$ and\n$$|R_{\\mu,\\delta}(g)-R_{\\mu_0,\\delta}(g)|\\le\\frac{2\\delta^2R}{a_0^2}W_1(\\mu,\\mu_0).$$",
