          "justified_by": [],
          "statement": "Assume countable choice. For a smooth oriented knot with a chosen product tubular neighbourhood $N(K)\\cong S^1\\times D^2$, let $\\mu$ be the positive fibre meridian and let $\\sigma$ be the product section $s\\mapsto(s,1)$ of $T_K=\\partial N(K)\\cong S^1\\times S^1$. Then $T_K=\\partial E_K$ is a torus and $[\\mu],[\\sigma]$ form a basis of $H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)$. The curve $\\sigma$ is a product section; this statement does not assert that it is the preferred zero-homology longitude.",
