          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice as in the maximal-abelian-cover convention. Let $L=K_1\\cup\\cdots\\cup K_r\\subset S^3$ be a nonempty oriented smooth link, with $r\\ge1$, compact exterior $E_L$ formed by deleting the interiors of pairwise-disjoint chosen closed normal-disk tubes, and basepoint $b\\in E_L$. For a knot, $r=1$ and $E_L=E_K$. The full meridian abelianization group is $H_L=H_1(E_L;\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\mathbb Z^r$, with the positive normal-disk meridians as its ordered basis. Choose a finite-rank free abelian group $H$ of positive rank and an epimorphism $\\chi:H_L\\to H$; write $\\psi=\\chi\\circ\\mathrm{ab}:G\\to H$ for the induced map from $G=\\pi_1(E_L,b)$. The identity choice $H=H_L$ is the full multivariable deck map; a coloring may identify its variables only through the explicitly stated map $\\chi$. Let $\\mathbb F$ be a field, let $d\\ge1$, and let $\\rho:G\\to\\mathrm{GL}_d(\\mathbb F)$ be a representation. Put $\\Lambda=\\mathbb F[H]$, the commutative Laurent-polynomial ring with monomial basis $H$, and $Q=\\operatorname{Frac}(\\Lambda)$. On row vectors define the right $\\mathbb F[G]$ action by $v\\cdot g=v\\rho(g)\\psi(g)$, where $\\psi(g)$ is central multiplication by its monomial in $\\Lambda$. For a chosen finite based CW structure $X$ on $E_L$, orient and order its cells and choose one lift of each cell to the universal cover $\\widetilde X$. The twisted cellular complex is\n\n$$C_*^{\\rho,\\psi}(X;\\Lambda^d)=\\Lambda^d\\otimes_{\\mathbb F[G]}C_*(\\widetilde X;\\mathbb F),$$\n\nand its fraction-field complex is $C_*^{\\rho,\\psi}(X;Q^d)=Q\\otimes_{\\Lambda}C_*^{\\rho,\\psi}(X;\\Lambda^d)$. The lifted cell bases and the standard coordinate basis of $\\mathbb F^d$ give the based $Q$-vector-space bases. If this fraction-field complex is not acyclic, define its twisted torsion to be $0$. If it is acyclic, choose in each degree a basis $\\mathbf b_i$ of $B_i=\\operatorname{im}\\partial_{i+1}$ and lifts $\\widetilde{\\mathbf b}_{i-1}$ of $\\mathbf b_{i-1}$ under $\\partial_i$; with $\\mathbf c_i$ the based cellular basis, set\n\n$$\\tau(C_*,\\mathbf c)=\\prod_i[\\mathbf b_i,\\widetilde{\\mathbf b}_{i-1}/\\mathbf c_i]^{(-1)^{i+1}}\\in Q^\\times,$$\n\nwhere brackets denote the determinant of the change-of-basis matrix. The twisted Reidemeister torsion is this value modulo the subgroup $\\mathcal U_{\\rho,\\psi}=\\{\\pm\\det(\\rho(g))\\psi(g)^d:g\\in G\\}\\subset Q^\\times$. This exact determinant image is contained in the commonly used coarser unit subgroup $\\{\\pm a h:a\\in\\det(\\rho(G)),\\ h\\in H\\}$. The choice-free statement uses the full abelianization chain model first and specializes it only by the declared coefficient map $\\chi$."
