          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice convention of the twisted-chain definition. Let $X$ be a connected finite based two-dimensional CW complex with one $0$-cell, $n\\ge2$ $1$-cells and $n-1$ $2$-cells, so $\\chi(X)=0$. Let $G=\\pi_1(X)$, let $\\psi:G\\twoheadrightarrow H\\cong\\mathbb Z^m$ be an epimorphism with $m\\ge1$, let $\\rho:G\\to\\mathrm{GL}_d(\\mathbb F)$ be a representation over a field $\\mathbb F$, set $\\Lambda=\\mathbb F[H]$ and $Q=\\operatorname{Frac}(\\Lambda)$, and give $\\Lambda^d$ the right $\\mathbb F[G]$-action $v\\cdot g=v\\rho(g)\\psi(g)$, with $\\psi(g)$ acting by its central monomial. Form\n\n$$C_*^{\\rho,\\psi}(X;\\Lambda^d)=\\Lambda^d\\otimes_{\\mathbb F[G]}C_*(\\widetilde X;\\mathbb F),$$\n\nwhere $\\widetilde X$ is the universal cover, and set $C_*^{\\rho,\\psi}(X;Q^d)=Q\\otimes_\\Lambda C_*^{\\rho,\\psi}(X;\\Lambda^d)$. If every element of $H_1(C_*^{\\rho,\\psi}(X;\\Lambda^d))$ is annihilated by some nonzero element of $\\Lambda$, then $C_*^{\\rho,\\psi}(X;Q^d)$ is acyclic. No assumption that its degree-two homology vanishes before localization is required."
