          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Nikolai Saveliev, Lectures on the Topology of 3-Manifolds, 2nd revised edition, Lecture 2 §2.2",
                "url": "https://poisson.phc.dm.unipi.it/~camponovo/libri/3mani.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Peter S. Ozsváth, András I. Stipsicz, and Zoltán Szabó, Heegaard Floer homology, version 2025-12-15, §1.2.3",
                "url": "https://web.math.princeton.edu/~petero/konyv9.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Mohamed Elhamdadi, Mustafa Hajij, and Kyle Istvan, Framed Knots, arXiv:1910.10257v6, §§4–7",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1910.10257v6"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented $3$-sphere, let $N(K)$ be a chosen closed tubular solid-torus neighborhood, let $E_K=\\overline{S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)}$, and let $T_K=\\partial E_K=\\partial N(K)$. Let $\\mu$ be the positive oriented meridian, meaning the boundary of a positive normal disk in $N(K)$, and let $\\lambda$ be a preferred longitude, meaning a degree-one parallel of the core $K$ in $N(K)$ that is null-homologous in $E_K$. Assume that $[\\mu],[\\lambda]$ are an ordered basis of $H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)$, with the boundary-orientation convention $\\mu\\cdot\\lambda=-1$. A slope is the unoriented isotopy class of an essential simple closed curve on $T_K$ whose homology class is $p[\\mu]+q[\\lambda]$ for coprime integers $p,q$ not both zero; $(p,q)$ and $(-p,-q)$ represent the same slope. For a slope represented by $p[\\mu]+q[\\lambda]$, the Dehn filling $E_K(p/q)$ is obtained by gluing an oriented solid torus $D^2\\times S^1$ to $E_K$ by an orientation-reversing boundary homeomorphism that sends $[\\partial D^2\\times\\{1\\}]$ to that slope; the filled orientation agrees with the fixed orientation on $E_K$. If $q\\ne0$, the coefficient is written $p/q$; the meridional slope is $1/0$, and integer $n$-framed filling means slope $n[\\mu]+[\\lambda]$. The oriented homeomorphism type is independent of the gluing map once its meridian image is fixed."
        },
