              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented $3$-sphere, choose a closed tubular neighborhood $N(K)$, and set $E_K=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)$ and $T_K=\\partial E_K=\\partial N(K)$; assume $E_K$ is connected. Let $\\mu$ be the oriented boundary of a normal disk whose orientation, preceded by the oriented tangent to $K$, agrees with the orientation of $S^3$. Let $\\lambda$ be a simple closed curve on $T_K$ whose degree under the normal-tube projection $T_K\\to K$ is $+1$ and whose image in $H_1(E_K;\\mathbb Z)$ is zero; such a curve is a preferred longitude. Assume $([\\mu],[\\lambda])$ is an ordered basis of $H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)$. For coprime integers $p,q$ not both zero, let $E_K(p/q)$ be the filling whose attached solid-torus meridian maps to $p[\\mu]+q[\\lambda]$. Then\n$$H_1(E_K(p/q);\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\begin{cases}\\mathbb Z/|p|\\mathbb Z,&p\\ne0,\\\\[2pt]\\mathbb Z,&p=0.\\end{cases}$$"
        },
