          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $M=H_-\\cup_\\varphi H_+$ be a Heegaard splitting of a closed oriented smooth $3$-manifold, let $\\Sigma=\\partial H_-=\\partial H_+$, and let $c\\subset\\Sigma$ be an embedded circle with a chosen annular neighbourhood. If $\\varphi$ is replaced by $\\varphi\\circ\\tau_c$ or $\\varphi\\circ\\tau_c^{-1}$, where $\\tau_c$ is a Dehn twist in the chosen annular coordinates, the resulting oriented $3$-manifold is obtained from $M$ by one surgery on a knot $K$ obtained by pushing $c$ into the interior of $H_-$. The annulus between $c$ and the boundary of a tubular neighbourhood of $K$ supplies a framing; the surgery meridian is identified with $\\mu+ \\lambda_A$ or $\\mu-\\lambda_A$, according to the twist direction, where $\\mu$ is the meridian of $K$ and $\\lambda_A$ is the parallel determined by that annulus. Thus the surgery coefficient relative to this framing is integral with absolute value $1$."
