          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $p,q\\ge2$ be coprime integers. There is a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface $F_{p,q}\\subset S^3$ whose oriented boundary is $T(p,q)$ and whose genus is $(p-1)(q-1)/2$. It can be constructed from a disk by plumbing $(p-1)(q-1)$ positive Hopf bands: a positive Hopf band is the oriented annulus spanning the positively linked Hopf link, and plumbing along a square glues square neighborhoods of properly embedded arcs in two surfaces on opposite sides of a 3-ball, with the four boundary edges alternating between the surfaces and with orientations agreeing on the square. For a connected compact oriented surface with one boundary component, genus is defined by $\\chi(F)=1-2g(F)$."
