          "statement": "Assume the full Axiom of Choice. A positive Hopf band is an oriented annulus with unknotted core whose two boundary components, with their induced orientations, have linking number $+1$. Let $F$ be the genus-one Seifert surface obtained by plumbing two positive Hopf bands in a square, with oriented core curves $a,b$ forming a positive handle basis, and choose the plumbing side so that $a^+$ bounds a disk in $S^3$ disjoint from $b$. The oriented boundary of this standard positive two-band plumbing is the right-handed trefoil. In the positive-push convention $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$ with ordered basis $(a,b)$, the Seifert matrix is\n$$\nV=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&0\\\\-1&-1\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n\nMore generally, the same matrix conclusion holds for any genus-one Seifert surface obtained by plumbing two oriented annuli with induced boundary linking number $+1$, provided their core curves form the stated positive handle basis and the stated disk for $a^+$ is disjoint from $b$. This broader matrix assertion does not identify the boundary knot."
