          ],
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "justified_by": [],
          "statement": "Let $X$ be a closed oriented Riemannian four-manifold and let $P\\to X$ be a smooth principal $SU(2)$-bundle with $c_2(P)[X]=-1$. The Hodge star on two-forms is $*$, and $F_A^-=(F_A-*F_A)/2$ denotes the anti-self-dual projection of the curvature of a connection $A$. The equation used in this item is $F_A^-=0$, so the curvature is self-dual; this convention and the negative second Chern number are fixed together for the positive-definite orientation. The self-dual moduli set is the set of smooth connections satisfying $F_A^-=0$, modulo the action of smooth gauge transformations of $P$. At a solution, the deformation complex is $0\\to\\Omega^0(X;\\operatorname{ad}P)\\xrightarrow{d_A}\\Omega^1(X;\\operatorname{ad}P)\\xrightarrow{d_A^-}\\Omega^-(X;\\operatorname{ad}P)\\to0$, and its gauge-fixed operator is $D_A=d_A^*\\oplus d_A^-$. For index calculations, $D_A$ is completed from the first Sobolev space of one-forms to the direct sum of the zeroth Sobolev spaces of zero-forms and anti-self-dual two-forms.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "strategy": "not-applicable",
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Simon K. Donaldson, An Application of Gauge Theory to the Topology of 4-Manifolds",
                "url": "https://webhomes.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/donaldson.pdf",
                "locator": "§§I.2 and II.1, printed pp. 282–287; sign convention $F_A^-=0$ and $c_2(P)[X]=-1$"
              }
            ]
          },
          "proof_strategy": "not-applicable"
