          "dependency_level": 0,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $\\mathcal C$ be a ribbon category with chosen left duals and tensor unit $\\mathbf 1$. A **finite oriented framed link colored in $\\mathcal C$** is a finite disjoint union $L$ of oriented smoothly embedded circles in $S^3$, a homotopy class of nowhere-zero normal vector field on each component, and an assignment of an object of $\\mathcal C$ to each component. A framed colored isotopy carries orientations, framings, and component colors. If $F_{\\mathcal C}$ is the ribbon-tangle evaluation functor, define\n$$\\operatorname{RT}_{\\mathcal C}(L):=F_{\\mathcal C}(L)\\in\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathcal C}(\\mathbf 1).$$\nThis value depends only on the framed colored isotopy class. It is not automatically a field scalar; if $\\mathcal C$ is $k$-linear and $\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathcal C}(\\mathbf 1)=k$, it is a scalar in $k$. The empty link is assigned $1_{\\mathbf 1}$.",
          "strategy": "Uses the complete multicolored ribbon-tangle evaluator, checks that a closed link has empty boundary and that framed isotopy preserves its value, and distinguishes End_C(1) from a field scalar.",
