          "statement": "The converse integration theorem is a separate established result: over $\\mathbb Q$, every unframed weight system is the top symbol of a finite-type knot invariant, by the Kontsevich integral. For every characteristic-zero field $k$, the same existence follows from the rational theorem by the finite-dimensional scalar-extension argument below. The Kontsevich integration proof itself belongs to the later authoring pair KT-35 and is not supplied here. This converse is not a premise for the KT-34 symbol theorem or its local relations, and it is an established theorem rather than an open problem."
