          "statement": "Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $n\\ge0$. In the unframed category, let $V$ be an $R$-valued invariant of type at most $n$. In the framed category assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ and let $V$ be an $R$-valued framed invariant of type at most $n$. In either category, every degree-$n$ chord diagram $D$ has an $n$-singular representative $K$ with no framing zeroes in the framed case, and $w_V(D):=D_nV(K)$ is independent of the representative and of its zero-free framing class. For every degree-$n$ 4T generator $D_1-D_2+D_3-D_4$, the induced values satisfy $w_V(D_1)-w_V(D_2)+w_V(D_3)-w_V(D_4)=0$; this holds in the framed category with no 1T condition."
