          },
          "statement": "Fix either a strict Morse presentation $K:S^1\\hookrightarrow\\mathbb C\\times\\mathbb R$ or a compact strict Morse tangle $T\\subset\\mathbb C\\times[a,b]$, and an integer $m\\ge1$. For each chamber of the ordered level simplex and each choice of the local branches paired at its levels, let $C_m$ be the resulting open configuration cell. The finite union of these cells has a compactification $\\overline C_m$ that is a compact manifold with corners. Its boundary strata record exactly: adjacent level collisions $t_i=t_{i+1}$; the endpoint faces at $t_{\\min},t_{\\max}$ for a knot or at $a,b$ for a tangle; levels reaching a critical value of the height function; and compatible intersections of these events. Whenever endpoint positions coalesce, real oriented blow-up records their relative scale and limiting direction, including nested collision clusters. The branch-evaluation maps extend smoothly to the resolved faces. Orient each open cell by $dt_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge dt_m$ and orient every new collision face by the outward-normal-first convention using its nonnegative radial coordinate; a critical-level face uses the local Morse coordinate $s\\ge0$ with $t-c=\\pm s^2$ and the same boundary-orientation convention.\n\nThe diagram shows the level simplex for $m=2$. Its diagonal is the equal-level face, the outer edges are the minimum/maximum endpoint faces, and the dashed cuts are critical levels; their intersections are the corner strata.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]\n  \\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\n  \\coordinate (B) at (3,0);\n  \\coordinate (C) at (3,3);\n  \\draw[thick] (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;\n  \\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,3.35) node[above] {$t_2$};\n  \\draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.35,0) node[right] {$t_1$};\n  \\draw[dashed] (0.6,0.5) -- (2.5,0.5) node[right] {$t_2=c$};\n  \\draw[dashed] (1.6,0) -- (1.6,1.6) node[above] {$t_1=c'$};\n  \\node at (2.1,1.05) {$t_2<t_1$};\n  \\node at (2.75,2.4) {$t_1=t_{\\max}$};\n  \\node at (0.85,0.22) {$t_2=t_{\\min}$};\n  \\node at (2.55,2.2) {$t_2=t_1$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n```"
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-kontsevich-morse-isotopy-decomposition",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Generic isotopies have finite Morse movies",
          "deps": [
            "def-kontsevich-integral-on-parenthesized-braids",
