          "statement": "Assume countable choice. Let $F\\subset B^4\\subset\\mathbb R^4$ be a compact connected oriented smoothly properly embedded surface of genus $g$, with its supplied smooth boundary collar and oriented boundary the knot $K\\subset S^3$. There is an orientation-preserving ambient diffeomorphism $\\Psi:B^4\\to B^4$ equal to the identity on a neighborhood of the outer boundary, and $0<\\varepsilon<1$, such that $\\Psi(F)\\cap B^4_\\varepsilon$ is exactly a flat two-disk in a plane through $0$. The surface $\\Psi(F)\\setminus\\operatorname{int}B^4_\\varepsilon$, in the explicitly round shell $B^4\\setminus\\operatorname{int}B^4_\\varepsilon\\cong S^3\\times[0,1]$, is a connected smooth oriented knot cobordism between $K$ and a standard unknot, with genus $g$ and Euler characteristic $-2g$. Both boundary components have product collars in a shell identification fixing $K$ and the inner sphere. The ambient diffeomorphism $\\Psi$ fixes a sufficiently small restriction of the supplied outer collar; the shell coordinates may be adjusted there to make that surface collar a product. No assertion about the complement of an arbitrary embedded four-ball is used.",
