          "statement": "Let $D$ be a finite regular oriented diagram of a link with $c$ components, and form its rational Lee cochain complex using the normalized crossing cube and decreasing quantum filtration. The associated bounded spectral sequence has the rational Khovanov cohomology of $D$ on its homology page and converges to the associated graded of Lee homology with its induced filtration. For the empty link, both rational complexes use the one-term empty tensor complex $\\mathbb Q$ in bidegree $(0,0)$ with zero differential, so the spectral sequence is constant. For each of the $2^c$ orientations $o$ of the link, let $D_o$ be the oriented resolution and set $a=1+X$ and $b=X-1$ in $A_L=\\mathbb Q[X]/(X^2-1)$. For each Seifert circle $C$ in $D_o$, let $\\delta(C)\\in\\mathbb Z/2\\mathbb Z$ be the parity of the number of other Seifert circles separating $C$ from infinity, and let $\\kappa(C)=1$ if $C$ is counterclockwise in the oriented projection plane and $\\kappa(C)=0$ if it is clockwise in that plane. Label $C$ by $a$ exactly when $\\delta(C)+\\kappa(C)$ is even, and by $b$ otherwise. These labels define a canonical Lee cycle $s_o$, and the cycles form a basis of Lee homology. For the empty link, its unique orientation class is the empty-tensor unit and spans its one-dimensional Lee homology. For a knot, the two canonical classes $s_o,s_{\\bar o}$ have equal least filtration level, while $s_o+s_{\\bar o}$ and $s_o-s_{\\bar o}$ are nonzero classes in the two distinct quantum-degree congruence summands modulo $4$.\n\n\n### Local crossing convention\n\nFor the proof’s local convention, the four segment ends are numbered clockwise, and sectors $(1,2)$ and $(3,4)$ are black. The textual endpoint and arrow rules in step 1.2 determine all labels; the drawing is illustrative and is not used in the proof.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1.1]\n  \\fill[black!18] (0,0) -- (0.72,0) arc (0:90:0.72) -- cycle;\n  \\fill[black!18] (0,0) -- (-0.72,0) arc (180:270:0.72) -- cycle;\n  \\node at (0.48,0.48) {$B$};\n  \\node at (-0.48,-0.48) {$B$};\n  \\draw[line width=5pt] (-0.8,0) -- (0.8,0);\n  \\draw[white,line width=5pt] (-0.2,0) -- (0.2,0);\n  \\draw[line width=1pt] (-0.8,0) -- (-0.2,0);\n  \\draw[line width=1pt] (0.2,0) -- (0.8,0);\n  \\draw[line width=1pt] (0,0.8) -- (0,-0.8);\n  \\node[above] at (0,0.82) {$1$};\n  \\node[right] at (0.82,0) {$2$};\n  \\node[below] at (0,-0.82) {$3$};\n  \\node[left] at (-0.82,0) {$4$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n```"
