          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $I^*$ be the binary icosahedral group, the group of $120$ unit quaternions acting on the unit sphere $S^3$ by left multiplication, and put $P=S^3/I^*$. The quotient is a closed connected oriented $3$-manifold with universal cover $S^3$ and deck group $I^*$. Then $H_*(P;\\mathbb Z)\\cong H_*(S^3;\\mathbb Z)$ and $\\pi_1(P)\\cong I^*$ is nontrivial.",
