          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "statement": "Let $F$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $\\rho:\\Gamma\\to SL_2(F)$ be a representation of a finitely generated group which is absolutely irreducible, meaning that no line is invariant under all its matrices after extension to any field containing $F$. Let $K\\subseteq F$ be the subfield generated by the prime field and all traces $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho(g)$, $g\\in\\Gamma$. There are words $A=\\rho(a)$ and $B=\\rho(b)$ and an element $\\xi$ satisfying $\\xi^2-(\\operatorname{tr}A)\\xi+1=0$, with $\\xi\\ne\\xi^{-1}$, such that over $F(\\xi)$ the representation is conjugate by a matrix in $GL_2(F(\\xi))$ to one whose generator matrices all lie in $SL_2(K(\\xi))$. Thus the required model field has degree at most two over $K$. The entries are obtained by explicit finite formulas from $\\xi$ and the traces of $A,B,AB,C,AC,BC,ABC$ for each generator matrix $C$. If $K(\\xi)\\ne K$, its nonidentity automorphism is realized on this model by simultaneous conjugation with one explicit matrix in $GL_2(K(\\xi))$. In particular, suppose a projective point $z\\in\\mathbb P^r(K(\\xi))$ is obtained from the model by a construction commuting with field automorphisms and invariant under simultaneous $GL_2$ conjugation. Then $z$ is defined over $K$. This last clause requires the stated compatibility and invariance; it asserts no analytic, homology-rank or quotient-existence theorem.",
