          "statement": "Assume full AC. Let $n\\ge0$, let $R_{\\mathbb Q}=\\mathbb Q[z_1^{\\pm1},\\ldots,z_n^{\\pm1}]$ and $R_{\\mathbb C}=\\mathbb C[z_1^{\\pm1},\\ldots,z_n^{\\pm1}]$, and let $I\\subseteq R_{\\mathbb C}$ be an ideal invariant under coefficientwise application of every field automorphism of $\\mathbb C$ fixing $\\mathbb Q$. Then $$I=(I\\cap R_{\\mathbb Q})R_{\\mathbb C}.$$ If $I$ is radical, then $I\\cap R_{\\mathbb Q}$ is radical as well. In particular, if $S\\subseteq(\\mathbb C^*)^n$ is preserved by all such coordinatewise automorphisms, the radical vanishing ideal of its Zariski closure is the scalar extension of a radical ideal over $\\mathbb Q$. This includes the empty set, the whole torus and zero variables. No algebraicity or closedness of $S$ is assumed.",
