          "axiom_use": "Choice-free; the filtration is finite and all arguments are degreewise.",
          "statement": "Let $(C,d,F)$ be a filtered chain complex over a field with an increasing filtration $0=F_{-1}C\\subseteq F_0C\\subseteq\\cdots\\subseteq F_nC=C$ and $d(F_pC)\\subseteq F_pC$. Its spectral sequence stabilizes and abuts to $H(C)$ with the image filtration, without any uniform bound outside the finite range $0\\le p\\le n$. If a particular filtered complex has been constructed from a fixed link diagram, this convergence assertion does not itself identify filtered complexes arising from different diagrams."
