          "statement": "Assume AC. Let $E\\to X$ be an oriented real vector bundle over a path-connected paracompact Hausdorff compactly generated weak Hausdorff space of CW homotopy type, and suppose one numerable Spin$^c$ lift of its oriented frame bundle is given. Among numerable Spin$^c$ lifts of that same frame bundle, isomorphism classes form a torsor for $H^2(X;\\mathbb Z)$: tensoring a lift by a complex line bundle defines a free and transitive action, identified with $H^2(X;\\mathbb Z)$ by the first Chern class. For a continuous map $f:X\\to Z$ between bases with these hypotheses and an oriented bundle $E_Z\\to Z$, the pullback action on lifts of $f^*E_Z\\to X$ is equivariant for $f^*:H^2(Z;\\mathbb Z)\\to H^2(X;\\mathbb Z)$.",
