          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. On the unit sphere $S^3\\subset\\mathbb R^4$ with height $h(x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4)=x_4$, let $c$ be a regular value and let $a$ be a smooth properly embedded arc in the upper ball $B_+=\\{x_4\\ge c\\}$, with endpoints on $S_c=\\{x_4=c\\}$, such that $h|_a$ has exactly one nondegenerate interior maximum and no other critical point. For every simple smooth arc $\\beta\\subset S_c$ joining those endpoints, there is an embedded disk in $B_+$ with boundary $a\\cup\\beta$. The corresponding statement for one nondegenerate minimum in the lower ball $B_-=\\{x_4\\le c\\}$ also holds."
