          ],
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "justified_by": [],
          "statement": "Assume countable choice, as required for the smooth normal-bundle structure in the tubular-neighbourhood interface. Let $K:S^1\\to S^3$ be a smooth oriented knot and let $\\nu(K)=TS^3|_K/TK$ be its quotient normal bundle. Equip $\\nu(K)$ with a chosen smooth fibre norm $\\|\\cdot\\|$. Let $\\Phi:\\Omega\\to S^3$ be a tubular-neighbourhood map from an open neighbourhood $\\Omega$ of the zero section in $\\nu(K)$ that restricts to the inclusion of $K$. For $\\epsilon>0$, define the closed disk subbundle\n$$\nD_\\epsilon\\nu(K):=\\{v\\in\\nu(K):\\|v\\|\\le\\epsilon\\}.\n$$\nChoose $\\epsilon$ so that $D_\\epsilon\\nu(K)\\subseteq\\Omega$, and set $N(K)=\\Phi(D_\\epsilon\\nu(K))$. The fibre norm, tubular map, and radius are part of the chosen tubular data. The **exterior** of this chosen tube is\n$$\nE_K:=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}_{S^3}N(K).\n$$\nRetain its boundary $T_K:=\\partial E_K=\\partial N(K)$, orient $E_K$ by restriction of the fixed orientation of $S^3$, and orient $T_K$ as the boundary of $E_K$. The choice of tubular map and radius is part of the input to this definition.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
