          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the standard oriented three-sphere $S^3$. A **Seifert surface** for $K$ is a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface $F\\subset S^3$ with boundary set equal to $K$. Orient each boundary component so that an outward-pointing conormal in $F$, followed by a positive boundary tangent, is a positive basis of $TF$; the oriented boundary of $F$ must agree with the given orientation of $K$. For such a surface, its genus $g(F)$ is the unique nonnegative integer satisfying $\\chi(F)=2-2g(F)-b$, where $b$ is the number of boundary components; here $b=1$, so $\\chi(F)=1-2g(F)$. The compact-surface normal-form result supplies this integer under the stated choice axiom."
