          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice convention of the twisted-chain definition. Let $L$ be a nonempty oriented link, let $E_L$ be its chosen compact exterior, and let $X$ be a finite based two-dimensional CW complex with one $0$-cell, $n\\ge2$ oriented $1$-cells $x_1,\\ldots,x_n$, and $n-1$ oriented $2$-cells attached by based words $r_1,\\ldots,r_{n-1}$. The supplied data include a based cellular spine certificate: a finite sequence of elementary cellular expansions and collapses identifying the simple-homotopy type of $X$ with the selected finite CW structure on $E_L$. Thus an abstract group isomorphism $\\pi_1(X)\\cong\\pi_1(E_L)$ alone is not a spine certificate. Let $G=\\pi_1(E_L)$, let $\\rho:G\\to\\mathrm{GL}_d(\\mathbb F)$ and $\\psi:G\\twoheadrightarrow H$ be the representation and declared free-abelian deck map, and put $Q=\\operatorname{Frac}(\\mathbb F[H])$. The associated deficiency-one presentation is $\\langle x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\mid r_1,\\ldots,r_{n-1}\\rangle$ through the certified spine map. For $w\\in F_n$, define Fox derivatives recursively by $\\partial x_k/\\partial x_j=\\delta_{kj}$, $\\partial(uv)/\\partial x_j=\\partial u/\\partial x_j+u\\,\\partial v/\\partial x_j$, and $\\partial x_k^{-1}/\\partial x_j=-x_k^{-1}\\delta_{kj}$. Extend them linearly to the group ring and let $\\Phi:\\mathbb F[F_n]\\to M_d(Q)$ be the ring homomorphism induced by $x_k\\mapsto\\rho(x_k)\\psi(x_k)$. Form the block Fox matrix $J=(\\Phi(\\partial r_i/\\partial x_k))_{i,k}$, of size $(n-1)d$ by $nd$. For a chosen column index $j$, let $J_{\\widehat j}$ be obtained by deleting its entire $d$-column block and let $D_j=\\det(\\rho(x_j)\\psi(x_j)-I_d)$. The Wada quotient for this column is defined only when $D_j\\ne0$, and then is $W_j=\\det(J_{\\widehat j})/D_j\\in Q$; a zero denominator makes that column inadmissible even when another column is valid. No abstract deficiency-one presentation is assigned exterior torsion unless its presentation complex is the stated based spine."
