          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K$ be the positively oriented trefoil, the closure of the positive two-strand braid $\\sigma_1^3$, and use the trivial one-dimensional representation and the single-color deck map sending each positive meridian to $t$. Use the standard genus-one Heegaard decomposition of $S^3$ with $K$ the $(2,3)$ curve on the splitting torus. Its two exterior pieces are solid tori meeting in an annulus whose core maps with degrees $2$ and $3$ to their oriented cores; the associated based simple-spine certificate has one vertex, core generators $a,b$, and one $2$-cell with attaching word $a^2b^{-3}$. The full abelianization sends $a$ to $t^3$ and $b$ to $t^2$. Deleting the $a$ column in this spine gives Wada quotient $-(t^4+t^2+1)/(t^3-1)=(t^2-t+1)/(1-t)$. In the cumulative-meridian basis, the reduced colored Burau block for $\\sigma_1$ is $[-t]$, so for $\\sigma_1^3$ it is $[-t^3]$; its numerator and boundary denominator are $-(t^3+1)$ and $t^2-1$. Their quotient is also $(t^2-t+1)/(1-t)$, the twisted torsion value for this based spine up to the declared units. Interpreting that ratio as the output of the full braid-axis procedure additionally requires the compatible axis-exterior and filling certificate in the procedure hypotheses.\n\nThe braid portion shown below uses the positive crossing convention from the colored procedure. The closure joins bottom endpoint $i$ to top endpoint $i$; because the endpoint permutation is a transposition, the closure is one component.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.8cm,line width=1pt]\n  \\node at (0,4.5) {$1$};\n  \\node at (1,4.5) {$2$};\n  \\node at (0,0.2) {$1$};\n  \\node at (1,0.2) {$2$};\n  % First positive crossing: left strand passes over right.\n  \\draw (0,4) -- (1,3);\n  \\draw (1,4) -- (0.58,3.58);\n  \\draw[white,line width=3pt] (0.42,3.42) -- (0,3);\n  \\draw (0.42,3.42) -- (0,3);\n  % Second positive crossing.\n  \\draw (0,3) -- (1,2);\n  \\draw (1,3) -- (0.58,2.5