          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the standard oriented $3$-sphere, choose its compact exterior $E_K$ with boundary torus $T_K$, and let $\\mu$ and $\\lambda$ be its positive meridian and preferred longitude. The exterior homology theorem gives $H_1(E_K;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z[\\mu]$. Let $\\phi:\\pi_1(E_K)\\to\\mathbb Z$ be the composite of abelianization with the homomorphism $[\\mu]\\mapsto1$. For an integer $q\\ge2$, let $\\phi_q$ be the composite $\\pi_1(E_K)\\xrightarrow{\\phi}\\mathbb Z\\to\\mathbb Z/q\\mathbb Z$, and let $p_q:E_q\\to E_K$ be the connected cover classified by $\\ker\\phi_q$. On $T_K$, the homomorphism sends $[\\mu]\\mapsto1$ and $[\\lambda]\\mapsto0$, so the preimage of $T_K$ is a connected torus cover whose fundamental group corresponds to $\\langle\\mu^q,\\lambda\\rangle$. Let $\\widetilde\\mu$ be the closed lift of $\\mu^q$. Attach a solid torus to $E_q$ with its meridian identified with $\\widetilde\\mu$; the resulting oriented closed $3$-manifold is the $q$-fold cyclic branched cover $\\Sigma_q(K)$. In tubular coordinates near $K$, the extended map to $S^3$ has local form $(s,w)\\mapsto(s,w^q)$, and the deck group $\\mathbb Z/q\\mathbb Z$ acts by $w\\mapsto e^{2\\pi i/q}w$.",
