          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K$ bound a connected compact oriented Seifert surface $F$ of genus $g$. Choose a disk-band decomposition of $F$ with one disk and $2g$ bands, and use its band-core basis $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ to form the positive-push Seifert matrix $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$. For $q\\ge2$, define the symmetric block matrix $M_q(V)$ of size $2g(q-1)$ by specifying its $2g\\times2g$ blocks, indexed by $1\\le k,\\ell\\le q-1$:\n$$(M_q(V))_{k\\ell}=\\begin{cases}V+V^T,&k=\\ell,\\\\-V^T,&\\ell=k+1,\\\\-V,&k=\\ell+1,\\\\0,&|k-\\ell|\\ge2.\\end{cases}$$\nPush the interior of $F$ into $B^4$ while keeping $K$ on $S^3=\\partial B^4$, and let $W_q(F)$ be the actual $q$-fold cyclic branched cover along that pushed-in surface. Use the following disk-band handle model of this cover. Cut $B^4$ along the three-dimensional track of the push-in isotopy; the cut-open manifold is again a $4$-ball and its boundary contains the thickened surface $\\bar F=(F\\times[-1,1])/\\sim$, where $(x,t)\\sim(x,t')$ for $x\\in\\partial F$. Write $\\bar F^\\pm=\\{(x,t)\\in\\bar F:\\pm t\\ge0\\}$. Take $q$ copies of this cut-open ball and, for $i=1,\\ldots,q-1$, glue $\\bar F_i^+$ to $\\bar F_{i+1}^-$ by $(x,t)\\mapsto(x,-t)$. The Akbulut–Kirby construction identifies this handle model with $W_q(F)$; the last-to-first gluing is unnecessary for the underlying manifold in this model. This is a statement about the isotopy-track handle model, not an assertion that an open chain of normal-disk sectors is already the cyclic covering map. The resulting handle presentation has one $0$-handle and $2g(q-1)$ $2$-handles, and its framed attaching link has linking matrix $M_q(V)$. The boundary branched cover, with the boundary marking induced by the covering map of $W_q(F)$, is $\\Sigma_q(K)$.",
