          "statement": "Assume full AC. Let $L=K_1\\cup\\cdots\\cup K_r\\subset S^3$ be a nonempty smooth oriented link, let $F$ be a compact smooth oriented embedded surface with oriented boundary $L$, and put $X=S^3\\setminus L$. For each component $K_i$, let $\\mu_i$ be the positive meridian, oriented as the boundary of a small normal disk so that a positive tangent to $K_i$ followed by the disk's positive basis gives the ambient orientation. Alexander duality identifies $H_1(X;\\mathbb Z)$ with the free abelian group on $[\\mu_1],\\ldots,[\\mu_r]$. Define the total-linking homomorphism $\\varphi:H_1(X;\\mathbb Z)\\to\\mathbb Z$ by $\\varphi(\\sum_i m_i[\\mu_i])=\\sum_i m_i$. If a smooth oriented loop $J\\subset X$ is transverse to the interior of $F$, define its signed intersection number $J\\cdot F$ by counting $+1$ when $J$ crosses from the negative to the positive side of the oriented normal of $F$ and $-1$ for the reverse crossing. Then $J\\cdot F=\\varphi([J])$.",
