          "statement": "Use the standard PL three-sphere given by the boundary of a fixed PL four-simplex and the product PL structure on $S^3\\times I$. A PL map is a map that is affine on every simplex after finite subdivisions of triangulated domain and target. An oriented PL knot is the image of a PL embedding of an oriented triangulated circle into this PL three-sphere. Two such knots are PL concordant when a PL embedding of a triangulated annulus into $S^3\\times I$ has them as its lower and upper boundary circles with boundary orientation $-K_0\\times\\{0\\}\\sqcup K_1\\times\\{1\\}$, and the embedding is proper, locally flat in the PL category, and has PL product collars agreeing with the ambient end products: for some $\\varepsilon>0$, its image near the lower end is $K_0\\times[0,\\varepsilon)$ and near the upper end is $K_1\\times(1-\\varepsilon,1]$. PL local-flatness means that each interior pair chart is PL-homeomorphic to $(\\mathbb R^4,\\mathbb R^2)$ and each boundary pair chart is PL-homeomorphic to $(\\mathbb R^4_+,\\mathbb R^2_+)$. Annuli with cone singularities or other non-locally-flat points are excluded. This definition makes no assertion identifying PL concordance with smooth or locally flat topological concordance."
