          "statement": "For each integer $n\\ge0$, let $S=\\mathbb Z[a^{\\pm1},z,d^{\\pm1}]/(z(d-1)-(a-a^{-1}))$ and $T=S[q^{\\pm1}]/(q-q^{-1}-z)$, with $z_D=q-q^{-1}$. Let $\\mathcal{KT}_n(T)$ be the ordinary Dubrovnik tangle skein algebra formed from regular-isotopy classes with crossing rule $D_+-D_-=z_D(D_0-D_\\infty)$, curl factors $a,a^{-1}$, and free-circle factor $d$, where $D_0$ is through and $D_\\infty$ is cup-cap. Number its $2n$ boundary endpoints in cyclic order as $1,2,\\ldots,n,\\bar n,\\ldots,\\bar2,\\bar1$. A connector is a perfect matching of these endpoints. Orient each open strand from its lower-numbered endpoint to its higher-numbered endpoint and order the open strands by their initial endpoints. Place the finitely many closed strands after the open strands in any fixed order, with a chosen orientation and initial point for each. A diagram is totally descending if, in this traversal order, the first branch encountered at each crossing is the overpassing branch. Then $\\mathcal{KT}_n(T)$ is spanned by one loop-free, self-crossing-free totally descending tangle for each connector. These representatives can have crossings between distinct strands; their crossing data are fixed by the total traversal order. For $n=0$ the single representative is the empty tangle, and for $n=1$ it is the straight strand.",
