          "dependency_level": 2,
          "statement": "Let $M$ and $N$ be smooth oriented $3$-manifolds, and let\n$f:M\\to N$ be an orientation-preserving diffeomorphism. Then\n$[L]\\mapsto[f(L)]$ induces an $R$-module isomorphism\n$f_*:\\mathcal K_A(M)\\to\\mathcal K_A(N)$. These maps respect identity\ndiffeomorphisms and composition.\n\nLet $\\Sigma$ be a compact oriented surface with a specified product collar\n$\\iota:\\Sigma\\times[0,1]\\hookrightarrow M$ whose lower face lies in\n$\\partial M$. Give $\\Sigma\\times[0,1]$ the orientation pulled back from $M$\nby $\\iota$; the skein module and stacking product below use this orientation.\nThe stacking product on\n$\\mathcal K_A(\\Sigma\\times[0,1])$ and collar gluing define a unital left\naction on $\\mathcal K_A(M)$: a closed framed link in the surface product is\nplaced in a sufficiently thin outer subcollar and united with a framed link\nin the interior of $M$. The action is independent of the thin-collar width,\nassociative, and natural under orientation-preserving diffeomorphisms that\nrespect the specified collars. Only closed framed links are glued; no relative\nboundary endpoints are part of this action.",
