          "statement": "For $q\\ge0$, let $\\widehat{\\mathcal A}_{\\mathbb C}(q)$ be the degreewise completion of the algebra generated by $t_{ij}=t_{ji}$ for $1\\le i<j\\le q$, with $[t_{ij},t_{kl}]=0$ for four distinct indices and $[t_{ij},t_{ik}+t_{jk}]=0$ for distinct $i,j,k$. The generator $t_{ij}$ is a chord joining strands $i,j$. Set $\\Omega_q=(2\\pi i)^{-1}\\sum_{i<j}t_{ij}\\,d\\log(z_i-z_j)$; tangential endpoint transport removes the local residue factors. For $1\\le i\\le q$, let $\\epsilon_i:\\widehat{\\mathcal A}_{\\mathbb C}(q)\\to\\widehat{\\mathcal A}_{\\mathbb C}(q-1)$ delete strand $i$ and kill any diagram with a chord endpoint on it. Let $\\Delta_i:\\widehat{\\mathcal A}_{\\mathbb C}(q)\\to\\widehat{\\mathcal A}_{\\mathbb C}(q+1)$ double strand $i$ into adjacent parallel copies and sum over all assignments of its chord endpoints to either copy. For $\\Phi$ on three strands, let $\\Phi_{ijk}$ relabel strands $1,2,3$ as $i,j,k$; $\\Phi\\otimes\\mathrm{id}$ and $\\mathrm{id}\\otimes\\Phi$ place the associator on the indicated three adjacent strands. Products stack from bottom to top, so the rightmost factor acts first. Put $R_{ij}:=\\exp(t_{ij}/2)$.\n\nLet $\\Phi_{\\mathrm{KZ}}$ be the regularized KZ transport changing the ordered binary parenthesization $((12)3)$ to $(1(23))$. It is invertible, obeys $\\Phi_{\\mathrm{KZ}}^{-1}=(\\Phi_{\\mathrm{KZ}})_{321}$ and $\\epsilon_i(\\Phi_{\\mathrm{KZ}})=1$, and satisfies the pentagon and two positive hexagon identities $(\\mathrm{id}\\otimes\\Phi)(\\Delta_2\\Phi)(\\Phi\\otimes\\mathrm{id})=(\\Delta_3\\Phi)(\\Delta_1\\Phi),\\qquad\\Delta_1R=\\Phi_{312}R_{13}\\Phi_{132}^{-1}R_{23}\\Phi,\\qquad\\Delta_2R=\\Phi_{231}^{-1}R_{13}\\Phi_{213}R_{12}\\Phi^{-1}.$\nHere $\\Phi=\\Phi_{\\mathrm{KZ}}$, and $\\Delta_1R$ (respectively $\\Delta_2R$) doubles the first (respectively second) strand of $R$. The negative hexagons are the inverse equations $\\Delta_1(R^{-1})=\\Phi^{-1}R_{23}^{-1}\\Phi_{132}R_{13}^{-1}\\Phi_{312}^{-1},\\qquad\\Delta_2(R^{-1})=\\Phi R_{12}^{-1}\\Phi_{213}^{-1}R_{13}^{-1}\\Phi_{231}$.\nRegularized KZ transports assigned to the same geometric parenthesized braid are independent of the sequence of parenthesization changes.\n\nThe diagram shows the five binary parenthesizations of four ordered strands and the associator rotations around the pentagon. It records the face labels used in the proof; the argument uses paths in configuration space.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9,thick]\n  \\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\n  \\coordinate (B) at (2.2,0);\n  \\coordinate (C) at (2.9,1.7);\n  \\coordinate (D) at (1.1,2.8);\n  \\coordinate (E) at (-0.7,1.7);\n  \\draw[->] (A)--node[midway,below] {$\\Delta_1\\Phi$} (B);\n  \\draw[->] (B)--node[midway,right] {$\\Delta_3\\Phi$} (C);\n  \\draw[->] (D)--node[midway,right] {$\\mathrm{id}\\otimes\\Phi$} (C);\n  \\draw[->] (E)--node[midway,above] {$\\Delta_2\\Phi$} (D);\n  \\draw[->] (A)--node[midway,left] {$\\Phi\\otimes\\mathrm{id}$} (E);\n  \\fill (A) circle (1.5pt); \\fill (B) circle (1.5pt);\n  \\fill (C) circle (1.5pt); \\fill (D) circle (1.5pt); \\fill (E) circle (1.5pt);\n  \\node[below] at (A) {$(((12)3)4)$};\n  \\node[below] at (B) {$((12)(34))$};\n  \\node[right] at (C) {$1(2(34))$};\n  \\node[above] at (D) {$1((23)4)$};\n  \\node[left] at (E) {$((1(23))4)$};\n  \\node at (1.1,1.25) {$K_4$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n```\n\nThe braid diagram records a positive crossing of strand 1 past the two-strand block $(2,3)$: the lower labels are the strand labels, height increases upward, and each bold right-bottom branch is the overstrand. The crossings occur in the order $(1,2)$ then $(1,3)$; the proof justifies the corresponding path homotopy independently of the drawing.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9,thick]\n  % Strand 1 passes under strands 2 and 3 in the two positive crossings.\n  \\draw (0,0)--(0.43,0.86);\n  \\draw (0.57,1.14)--(0.93,1.86);\n  \\draw (1.07,2.14)--(2,4);\n  \\draw[very thick] (1,0)--(0.5,1)--(0