                "title": "Introduction to Vassiliev Knot Invariants, §§3.4 and 4.1–4.2",
                "url": "https://www.math.cinvestav.mx/~mostovoy/cdbook/cdbook-as-submitted.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Assume countable choice. The framed self-linking number of a framed oriented knot is the linking number of the knot with a sufficiently small push-off along its framing. Let $D_1$ be the degree-one chord diagram consisting of an oriented circle with one chord. The framed self-linking invariant has a degree-one weight system $w$ with $w(D_1)=2$. Since $D_1$ is isolated, the unframed 1T quotient sets it to zero. Therefore $w$ does not factor through the unframed 4T+1T quotient. This counterexample distinguishes the framed and unframed diagram targets and makes no claim about separating knot types.\n\nThe diagram shows the isolated one-chord generator; the circle orientation fixes its cyclic skeleton and no proof relies on the picture.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9,thick]\n  \\draw (0,0) circle (1);\n  \\draw[->] (0.05,0.99) .. controls (0.28,0.96) and (0.47,0.87) .. (0.60,0.80);\n  \\draw[very thick] ({cos(55)},{sin(55)}) -- ({cos(235)},{sin(235)});\n  \\fill ({cos(55)},{sin(55)}) circle (1.5pt);\n  \\fill ({cos(235)},{sin(235)}) circle (1.5pt);\n  \\node at (0,-1.35) {$D_1$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n```"
        },
