          "statement": "Let $Y$ be a closed connected oriented $3$-manifold, let $K\\subset Y$ be a smooth oriented null-homologous knot, and let $F\\subset Y$ be a compact connected oriented embedded surface with oriented boundary $K$. Choose a closed tubular neighborhood $N(K)$, put $M=Y\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)$, and let $\\gamma_\\mu$ be the union of two disjoint annuli on $\\partial M$ whose core sutures are parallel meridians of $K$ with opposite orientations. Delete a collar of $\\partial F$ to regard $F$ as a properly embedded surface in $(M,\\gamma_\\mu)$, with relative class $[F]\\in H_2(M,\\partial M;\\mathbb Z)$. Let $t_\\mu$ be the meridional boundary trivialization of the oriented plane field used in the relative Spin-c definition. For $\\mathfrak{s}\\in\\operatorname{Spin}^c(M,\\gamma_\\mu)$, its Alexander grading is\n\n$$A_F(\\mathfrak{s})=\\frac12\\left\\langle c_1(\\mathfrak{s},t_\\mu),[F]\\right\\rangle,$$\n\nwith the standard sign convention that gives the usual Alexander grading for knots in $S^3$. For a balanced admissible sutured Heegaard diagram of $(M,\\gamma_\\mu)$, the Spin-c summand $SFH(M,\\gamma_\\mu,\\mathfrak{s};\\mathbb Z)$ is the homology of the integral sutured Floer disk-count complex generated by the Heegaard generators assigned to $\\mathfrak{s}$. Define the integral knot Floer group in Alexander grading $i$ by\n\n$$\\widehat{\\mathrm{HFK}}(Y,K,[F],i;\\mathbb Z)=\\bigoplus_{\\substack{\\mathfrak{s}\\in\\operatorname{Spin}^c(M,\\gamma_\\mu)\\\\ A_F(\\mathfrak{s})=i}}SFH(M,\\gamma_\\mu,\\mathfrak{s};\\mathbb Z).$$\n\nThis fixes the integral coefficient convention. The equivalent associated-graded closed Heegaard-complex presentation, invariance under changing diagrams, and comparison with the mod-two grid complex are separate theorems; this definition supplies none of their proofs or a coefficient-change map."
