          "statement": "Let $T$ be the trefoil represented by the standard oriented three-crossing diagram below. Choose a basepoint $x_0\\in S^3\\setminus T$ in the diagram's upper collar and use the common upper-collar paths from $x_0$ to base the positive-meridian generators. Its under-arcs are labelled $a,b,c$ so that the ordered triples $(o,L,R)$ of over-arc, upper target under-arc and lower source under-arc are $(b,c,a)$, $(c,a,b)$, and $(a,b,c)$ at the three crossings; read each triple in the orientation-preserving local chart that straightens the over-arc to point rightward. The knot group $G_T=\\pi_1(S^3\\setminus T,x_0)$, where $\\pi_1$ is based loops modulo endpoint-fixed homotopy with multiplication by concatenation, has presentation $\\langle a,b\\mid aba=bab\\rangle$. This presentation denotes the free group on $a,b$ modulo the normal closure of the displayed relation. Its abelianization, the quotient by its commutator subgroup, is isomorphic to $\\mathbb Z$, but $G_T$ is nonabelian.\n\nThe drawing shows two oriented strands crossing three times; the two bottom endpoints join to the corresponding top endpoints by the outside arcs. The white gaps mark underpasses, and each redrawn strand is over. The crossing triples in the statement fix the generator labels and local chart convention.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,>=stealth]\n\\foreach \\j in {0,1,2} {\n\\draw[->] (-1,3-\\j)--(-0.14,2.57-\\j);\n\\draw[->] (0.14,2.43-\\j)--(1,2-\\j);\n\\draw[->,line width=1.2pt] (1,3-\\j)--(-1,2-\\j);\n}\n\\draw[->] (-1,0)..controls(-1.7,0)and(-1.7,3)..(-1,3);\n\\draw[->] (1,0)..controls(1.7,0)and(1.7,3)..(1,3);\n\\node[above] at (-1,3) {$a$};\n\\node[above] at (1,3) {$b$};\n\\node[right] at (1,2) {$c$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n```"
