          "id": "lem-connected-plane-multigraph-euler-formula",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Euler formula for connected plane multigraphs",
          "statement": "Let $G$ be a finite nonempty connected plane multigraph drawn in $\\mathbb R^2$: vertices\nare distinct points; each edge is a polygonal arc joining its endpoints; edge\ninteriors are pairwise disjoint and avoid every vertex; and loops and parallel\nedges are allowed. A loop is an edge whose two endpoints are the same vertex,\nwith its interior otherwise embedded. A face is a connected component of the\ncomplement of the drawing. If $V,E,F$ are the numbers of vertices, edges, and\nfaces, respectively, then\n\n$$V-E+F=2.$$",
          "deps": [
            "def-plane-graph-face-and-boundary",
            "thm-euler-formula-for-connected-plane-graphs"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "strategy": "Subdivide each loop and each parallel edge twice using fresh vertices. The point-set drawing and faces stay fixed, while the resulting graph is finite, simple, connected, and plane; compare its vertex and edge counts with the original.",
          "sources": {
