          "statement": "Assume countable choice. Let a compact embedded surface in a smooth three-manifold have a supplied finite whole-star piecewise smooth triangulation: its simplex maps extend smoothly, and their differential fan is injective on the entire tangent star at every point. Suppose its boundary has an already smooth embedded collar in the surface. Then the surface can be replaced, in any prescribed neighborhood and fixed on a smaller boundary collar, by a smooth embedded surface homeomorphic to it relative to that collar. The replacement can also be fixed on any specified compact subset on a neighborhood of which the surface is already smooth. In particular an embedded disk with such data and smooth boundary collar has a smooth embedded disk replacement with exactly the same boundary.\n\nA finite PL surface in the compatible PL structure of a supplied whole-star smooth triangulation of the ambient manifold has the required piecewise smooth data after common subdivision. This clause concerns compatibility with the specified smooth triangulation; it does not assert compatibility of an arbitrary topological marking.",
