          "statement": "Assume countable choice. Let $K:S^1\\to S^3$ be a smooth oriented knot with a supplied product tubular neighborhood, and let $E_K$ be its compact exterior with peripheral torus $T_K$, fibre meridian $\\mu$, and the unique degree-one generator $[\\lambda]$ of the kernel of $H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)\\to H_1(E_K;\\mathbb Z)$ supplied by the product-tube Mayer–Vietoris calculation. Then $K$ is ambient isotopic in the smooth category to the standard unknot if and only if $E_K$ contains a properly embedded piecewise-linear disk $D$ whose boundary is not null-homotopic in $T_K$. Every such disk has $[\\partial D]=[\\lambda]$ or $-[\\lambda]$ and has odd mod-two intersection with the original marked meridian $\\mu$.",
