          "statement": "Assume AC. Let a nonempty labeled oriented closed link have a based regular diagram with an underpass on every component. Choose an initial arc on each component, its positive meridian $x_i$, and the common upper basing. Put $F=\\langle x_1,\\ldots,x_r\\rangle$ and $G=\\pi_1(E_L)$. For every $q\\ge2$ there are explicit words $l_{i,q}\\in F$ representing the preferred longitudes in $G/\\Gamma_qG$ such that the meridian map identifies\n$$G/\\Gamma_qG\\cong F/\\langle\\!\\langle\\Gamma_qF,[x_i,l_{i,q}]\\ (1\\le i\\le r)\\rangle\\!\\rangle.$$\nThe words can be chosen coherently through each finite degree. They are obtained through the $(q-1)$st approximation of the crossing-conjugation recursion, initialized by component meridians and using the preceding approximation for every over-arc. In particular this describes the kernel, rather than merely the surjectivity, of the component-meridian map. Quotienting further by commutators of arbitrary conjugates of each component meridian adds exactly those commutators to this presentation.",
